1
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:50,380
(Shen Teng)

2
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:52,940
(Bai Jingting)

3
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:54,980
(Jia Bing)

4
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:57,340
(Hu Xianxu)

5
00:01:00,020 --> 00:01:01,740
(Wang Anyu)

6
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:04,020
(Fan Chengcheng)

7
00:01:04,380 --> 00:01:06,180
(Huang Jingyu)

8
00:01:06,580 --> 00:01:08,260
(Wang Churan)

9
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:13,820
=Natural High S4=

10
00:01:18,780 --> 00:01:22,820
How does life flow?

11
00:01:22,820 --> 00:01:25,020
Powerful.

12
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:27,920
It's so beautiful.

13
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:29,200
Look at the huge waterfall.

14
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:29,880
It's magnificent.

15
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:30,840
What a beautiful waterfall.

16
00:01:31,340 --> 00:01:33,980
Peaceful.

17
00:01:34,720 --> 00:01:35,840
The water is so clear.

18
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:37,480
It's so blue.

19
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:39,520
It's gorgeous.

20
00:01:41,660 --> 00:01:43,460
Lively.

21
00:01:49,250 --> 00:01:50,870
Turbulently.

22
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:52,160
Let's go!

23
00:01:56,920 --> 00:01:59,040
(Ocean, Waterfalls, Valleys, Rainforests)
This time, we follow the water

24
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:01,160
through its many different forms

25
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:03,040
to discover the different ways
life thrives.

26
00:02:05,480 --> 00:02:07,640
Waves keep crashing against the shore.

27
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
In the rainforest, vines climb up trees.

28
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,640
They keep growing

29
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:14,920
with amazing strength.

30
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:18,660
(Shen Teng)

31
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,160
I really love the ocean.

32
00:02:20,160 --> 00:02:21,480
(Wang Anyu)
And I love trees.

33
00:02:21,480 --> 00:02:24,400
Whenever I'm surrounded
by forests and the ocean,

34
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:26,280
I feel relaxed.

35
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:29,840
I think reconnecting with nature

36
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,200
(Bai Jingting)
can be incredibly energizing.

37
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,160
You get to experience nature,

38
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:34,360
feel the sunshine,

39
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,880
get away from the city,

40
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:38,080
and take in the natural world firsthand.

41
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:39,600
To me, the vitality of nature

42
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:42,200
(Fan Chengcheng)
lies in the surprises

43
00:02:42,200 --> 00:02:43,520
and beauty it brings.

44
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:44,480
Don't overthink things
or wear yourself out.

45
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:46,200
Just focus on growing.

46
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:47,240
I think nature is always filled

47
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:50,160
(Hu Xianxu)
with new life and death.

48
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:52,920
The sun will always rise as usual.

49
00:02:52,920 --> 00:02:54,040
Everything in the world

50
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:56,760
continues to go through endless cycles.

51
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:58,760
I find that incredibly powerful.

52
00:02:59,360 --> 00:03:01,440
(Jia Bing)
We have a new member this year.

53
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:04,080
We're gradually bringing in fresh blood.

54
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,240
I think

55
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:07,240
that's a wonderful sign of vitality.

56
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:09,880
(Wang Churan)
I think

57
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:11,440
when life gets you stuck,

58
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:13,000
you can always head out into nature,

59
00:03:13,000 --> 00:03:13,680
sit down for a while,

60
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:15,440
take in the mountains and the water,

61
00:03:15,880 --> 00:03:17,640
and watch things flow.

62
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,840
I think that can help you
find your balance again.

63
00:03:20,680 --> 00:03:22,640
(Huang Jingyu)
Just put on a pair of fins and dive in.

64
00:03:22,640 --> 00:03:25,840
I love the freedom of diving this way.

65
00:03:25,840 --> 00:03:27,160
You can swim

66
00:03:27,160 --> 00:03:28,160
through the ocean

67
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:30,120
and explore alongside the fish.

68
00:03:30,120 --> 00:03:32,480
It's an amazing feeling.

69
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:33,760
You have to keep pushing your limits

70
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:35,400
to discover

71
00:03:35,400 --> 00:03:37,200
even more incredible sights.

72
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:40,000
The waves

73
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,200
wash all your worries away.

74
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,760
You get to see old friends again,

75
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:44,360
and it feels just like old times.

76
00:03:44,360 --> 00:03:45,640
It's so beautiful!

77
00:03:45,640 --> 00:03:47,240
It's so adorable!

78
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:48,280
Let's run over there in one go.

79
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:49,400
As easy as walking on flat ground.

80
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,440
It feels like we've signed up

81
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:51,760
for a senior citizens' tour.

82
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:54,320
It feels like we're inside a microwave.

83
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:55,560
Let's set off now!

84
00:03:55,960 --> 00:03:58,960
Now!

85
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:01,440
Let's set off now!

86
00:04:06,080 --> 00:04:08,160
Our first stop is the beautiful

87
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:09,160
(Hainan, Sanya, Wuzhizhou Island)
Wuzhizhou Island.

88
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:12,080
Overfishing

89
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,480
and land pollution

90
00:04:14,080 --> 00:04:15,760
severely degraded the coral reefs

91
00:04:15,760 --> 00:04:17,200
around Wuzhizhou Island.

92
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:18,320
Coral coverage

93
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:20,240
once dropped below 15%.

94
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:22,560
Since 2010,

95
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:25,200
marine ranches have been developed

96
00:04:25,200 --> 00:04:28,200
by adding artificial reefs
and sunken ships

97
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:31,000
to create new homes for marine life.

98
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,760
Let's dive into the blue ocean

99
00:04:33,760 --> 00:04:35,880
and build a home for marine creatures.

100
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:38,940
=EP1 (Part 1): A Glimpse of Blue=

101
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:42,320
Let's go!

102
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,960
Time to get in the water!

103
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:45,360
First time.

104
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:47,200
Starting a show barefaced
in such a tight outfit.

105
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:47,680
Right.

106
00:04:47,680 --> 00:04:48,760
Making an entrance in a wetsuit!

107
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:55,120
No, you go over there.

108
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:55,840
Jingyu, you don't need to sit down.

109
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:56,840
Just stand over there.

110
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:01,220
(The coaching team)

111
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:02,400
The coaches are all ready.

112
00:05:02,400 --> 00:05:03,760
Everyone needs to take their baby corals

113
00:05:03,760 --> 00:05:05,240
underwater for planting.

114
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:06,120
Thank you.

115
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:07,920
It's so tiny!

116
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:08,640
It'll grow.

117
00:05:09,200 --> 00:05:10,760
It's so small.

118
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,560
It'll grow bigger.

119
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,520
It's like planting a seed.

120
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:15,920
Everyone, let me go over the precautions

121
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:17,190
before we dive underwater.

122
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:18,080
(Huang Jingyu)
Everyone must remove their makeup

123
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:20,000
and sunscreen before diving.

124
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:21,280
(Tip: Harmful chemicals)
The chemicals

125
00:05:21,280 --> 00:05:22,400
(Everyone is makeup-free)
can cause coral bleaching,

126
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:23,840
(can bleach coral, harm larvae)
deform or kill coral larvae.

127
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:24,600
(and disrupt fish hormones)
Next,

128
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,960
let's talk about how
to plant coral underwater.

129
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:28,920
We set up

130
00:05:28,920 --> 00:05:29,640
these frames

131
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:31,240
(Jia Bing)
for our coral nursery.

132
00:05:31,240 --> 00:05:32,880
Each of us will have a cable tie.

133
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:34,360
Position the coral
with its front side facing up,

134
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:36,280
(Step 1: Dive underwater)
wrap the tie around it

135
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:37,600
(Step 2: Secure the coral to the frame)
and cross the ends over each other.

136
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:38,800
That will hold it firmly in place.

137
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,120
Once it's secured tightly
against the frame,

138
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:41,080
it will grow

139
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:42,360
and attach itself to the structure.

140
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:43,320
We're all set.

141
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:44,480
Okay, let's

142
00:05:45,320 --> 00:05:45,680
head out.

143
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,520
Wait, hold on!

144
00:05:46,520 --> 00:05:48,560
Nobody's taught us how to dive yet!

145
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:49,080
Just get in the water.

146
00:05:49,080 --> 00:05:50,720
You'll figure it out
once you're down there.

147
00:05:52,280 --> 00:05:54,920
Your survival instincts
will teach you how to dive.

148
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,640
We're only learning how to plant coral.

149
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:57,800
(Hu Xianxu)

150
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:59,360
They skipped the first step!

151
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:01,000
The coral's survival comes first.

152
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,240
Whether you make it or not
is another story.

153
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:04,280
Hu will be planting coral.

154
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,080
Then suddenly float back up.

155
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:08,960
The coaches will make sure

156
00:06:08,960 --> 00:06:09,480
you're safe

157
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:10,600
and show you exactly

158
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:11,600
how to move around underwater

159
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:12,720
with some simple swimming techniques.

160
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:13,440
(Relieved)
Got it.

161
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,160
Okay.

162
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:16,880
My ears start hurting
when I dive below three meters.

163
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:17,520
Neither of us can do it.

164
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:18,200
I'll stay with Bai.

165
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:20,200
He has a perforated eardrum.

166
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:22,440
(Bai Jingting)
We have Jiaozi submersible

167
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:23,760
(Can't dive due to ear pressure)
that can take you underwater.

168
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:25,200
(They'll ride in the Jiaozi submersible)
You can watch them

169
00:06:25,200 --> 00:06:26,280
planting coral.

170
00:06:26,280 --> 00:06:26,880
Okay.

171
00:06:27,560 --> 00:06:28,080
Let's go!

172
00:06:28,080 --> 00:06:29,640
Bing, I'm counting on you to plant mine!

173
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:30,040
Sure.

174
00:06:31,120 --> 00:06:32,540
I'll plant it for Bai.

175
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:33,660
Thanks, Teng!

176
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:35,520
These two are for Bai and me.

177
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:37,800
This one looks good.

178
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,120
Really?

179
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:40,040
You've got experience.

180
00:06:41,080 --> 00:06:41,600
A real pro.

181
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:44,180
Real pro.

182
00:06:44,240 --> 00:06:44,720
A real pro.

183
00:06:44,720 --> 00:06:46,160
We're up against another expert!

184
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:47,360
We're done for this round!

185
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:50,000
(Wang Anyu)
Let me show you

186
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,000
the circular breathing technique.

187
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:52,400
What a pro!

188
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:53,680
You've put your wetsuit on backward.

189
00:06:56,320 --> 00:06:57,440
I did put it on backward the first time.

190
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:58,480
The zipper goes in the front.

191
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:00,800
Churan did the same thing.

192
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:01,720
She was wondering

193
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:02,880
why she couldn't bend her legs.

194
00:07:03,760 --> 00:07:05,440
I was wondering
why I couldn't bend my legs.

195
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:10,400
Why isn't this sticking to my face?

196
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:13,440
Wang Anyu.

197
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:14,760
You're the expert.

198
00:07:14,820 --> 00:07:15,700
(Asking an expert for help)

199
00:07:15,720 --> 00:07:16,640
Is it supposed to stick to my face?

200
00:07:16,640 --> 00:07:17,160
Yes, it should.

201
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:18,520
Pull it a little tighter.

202
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,400
Is it sticking to your face now?

203
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:31,680
Is it sticking to your face?

204
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:32,760
It's touching your face now, right?

205
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:33,760
It's sealed against your face, right?

206
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,400
No, it's sticking to my face
too much now!

207
00:07:37,440 --> 00:07:38,280
You don't need this.

208
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:39,600
There's no point attaching it here.

209
00:07:39,600 --> 00:07:40,540
Once you're underwater, you won't...

210
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:43,340
(There'll be someone to protect you)

211
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:45,240
Mr. Huang, please try not to touch me.

212
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:51,680
You have to be a member to see his back.

213
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:52,880
It's so hot!

214
00:07:52,880 --> 00:07:54,480
(VIP exclusive)
It's way too hot along the way!

215
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:57,720
(Fan Chengcheng)
How much to unlock the back-view bonus?

216
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:59,720
You can even carve your own name here.

217
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:02,400
You have to unzip it a little.
That's a member perk.

218
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,400
This works too.

219
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:07,760
What are you doing?

220
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:11,120
This is for WeTV VIP members.

221
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,640
(VIP exclusive)

222
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:15,040
How much do you have to spend
to see the back?

223
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:16,360
Just pay for a membership!

224
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:18,080
Hurry, zip it back up!

225
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,040
Let's go!

226
00:08:23,280 --> 00:08:24,400
Let's go. You and me. I'll...

227
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:25,440
Can I give him a ride?

228
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:27,720
You drive the sub.

229
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:28,640
We... We can...

230
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:29,040
I'll drive the sub!

231
00:08:33,540 --> 00:08:35,300
(Starting the dive)

232
00:08:35,680 --> 00:08:36,880
It's like putting on a backpack.

233
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:37,800
Put the gear on your back.

234
00:08:37,800 --> 00:08:38,560
(Equipment setup: 1. Put on the mask)

235
00:08:38,570 --> 00:08:39,260
(2. Put on the scuba gear)

236
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:45,080
(3. Put the regulator in your mouth)
Breathe through your mouth.

237
00:08:45,080 --> 00:08:45,920
The device on your right

238
00:08:45,920 --> 00:08:47,200
is the regulator.

239
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:48,960
(Regulator. Shen Teng)
Bite down on the mouthpiece

240
00:08:48,960 --> 00:08:50,400
and seal your lips
around the outside in an O shape.

241
00:08:51,120 --> 00:08:53,000
(Breathe through your mouth. Wang Churan)
Breathe in deeply and exhale slowly.

242
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,380
Exhale completely
before breathing in again.

243
00:08:54,460 --> 00:08:57,220
(Hu Xianxu)

244
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:59,440
(Shen Teng)
If you feel uncomfortable underwater,

245
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:00,800
(Ascent signal)
signal the coach to bring you up.

246
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:02,840
The coach will bring you
to the surface right away.

247
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:03,600
If you're feeling fine,

248
00:09:03,600 --> 00:09:04,520
(Shen Teng)
the coach will signal you.

249
00:09:04,520 --> 00:09:06,080
(Okay signal)
Signal back to show you're okay.

250
00:09:06,620 --> 00:09:08,420
(The entire diving team is underwater)

251
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,200
So this is the submersible, right?

252
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:13,020
(Jiaozi: A small domestic
passenger sightseeing submersible)

253
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:14,280
Be careful going down.

254
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:15,280
You can step on it.

255
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:17,080
Bai, come on!

256
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:18,160
This is so cool!

257
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:22,440
This isn't what I expected.

258
00:09:23,040 --> 00:09:24,320
(Fan Chengcheng filming)
I'm riding in a submersible

259
00:09:24,320 --> 00:09:25,580
with a "superhero".

260
00:09:25,620 --> 00:09:26,570
(We don't play)

261
00:09:26,570 --> 00:09:27,500
(Keep it real)

262
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:31,220
(Fan Chengcheng filming)

263
00:09:32,420 --> 00:09:33,980
(Jiaozi submersible setting off)

264
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:36,640
Cool.

265
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:38,840
It'd be a shame not to ride this thing.

266
00:09:38,860 --> 00:09:42,940
(Bai Jingting filming)

267
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:44,900
(Jiaozi submersible descending)

268
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:45,960
We're completely underwater now.

269
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:46,440
Yeah.

270
00:09:48,240 --> 00:09:49,080
It's so clear!

271
00:09:50,480 --> 00:09:51,360
An underwater world on the move.

272
00:09:51,360 --> 00:09:52,040
Little fish!

273
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,160
Sea cucumbers!

274
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:00,080
There are so many sea cucumbers!

275
00:10:05,920 --> 00:10:06,880
Who's that?

276
00:10:07,260 --> 00:10:07,820
(Fan Chengcheng filming)

277
00:10:07,820 --> 00:10:08,880
(A giant "Jingyu" underwater)
[*Whale]

278
00:10:08,880 --> 00:10:09,600
Look!

279
00:10:09,600 --> 00:10:10,360
"The sea monster"!

280
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:13,920
"The sea monster" is here!

281
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:16,280
He's not using scuba gear!

282
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:20,020
(Huang Jingyu opts for freediving)

283
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:23,900
(Fan Chengcheng filming)

284
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:24,840
Absolutely gorgeous!

285
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:28,360
Who's that?

286
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:32,580
(Shen Teng)

287
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:33,200
Teng.

288
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:36,000
Teng kind of looks like

289
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,380
a beluga whale!

290
00:10:37,380 --> 00:10:39,820
(Shen Teng)

291
00:10:39,900 --> 00:10:42,180
(Hu Xianxu)

292
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:44,260
(Wang Anyu)

293
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:46,220
(Jia Bing)

294
00:10:46,260 --> 00:10:48,260
(Wang Churan)

295
00:10:48,520 --> 00:10:50,440
Are they supposed
to plant the coral on this?

296
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:51,000
Looks like

297
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:53,100
(Bai Jingting filming)
they should all be tied to it.

298
00:10:53,100 --> 00:10:54,580
(Coral nursery)

299
00:10:54,620 --> 00:10:56,730
(Everyone arrives at the planting site)

300
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:57,880
Let's go!

301
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:00,920
Time to start planting!

302
00:11:00,940 --> 00:11:03,500
(Shen Teng starts planting coral)

303
00:11:03,540 --> 00:11:05,780
(Wang Anyu)

304
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:08,120
I'd never even heard

305
00:11:08,120 --> 00:11:09,360
of coral planting before.

306
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:11,240
It's nice to have fun

307
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,040
while doing something

308
00:11:12,360 --> 00:11:14,300
(Hu Xianxu)
that we'll remember forever.

309
00:11:14,500 --> 00:11:15,900
(Wang Anyu)

310
00:11:15,940 --> 00:11:17,140
(Jia Bing)

311
00:11:17,160 --> 00:11:19,520
We've left our mark on the ocean floor

312
00:11:19,520 --> 00:11:22,000
(Wang Churan)
here in Sanya.

313
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,840
Hopefully, when we come back,

314
00:11:23,840 --> 00:11:25,940
the coral we planted

315
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:27,520
(Shen Teng)
will have grown

316
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:30,520
(Wang Anyu)
big and strong,

317
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:32,320
(Wang Churan)
with lots of little fish living among it

318
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:33,960
and a healthier environment

319
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:35,840
for them to thrive in.

320
00:11:36,500 --> 00:11:38,060
(Planting coral, nurturing new life)

321
00:11:38,060 --> 00:11:39,780
(May life flourish
beneath the blue waves)

322
00:11:41,560 --> 00:11:42,480
Who's that?

323
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:45,140
(It's "Jingyu" again)
[*Whale]

324
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,080
A fish that rides the waves!

325
00:11:47,520 --> 00:11:49,000
This is good!

326
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:49,720
He looks like...

327
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:50,680
That's so weird!

328
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:53,480
It feels like we're watching a show
at an aquarium.

329
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:55,140
("Jingyu" show)
[*Whale]

330
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:56,600
His move is pretty good.

331
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:57,840
Is that thing giving him a boost?

332
00:11:58,200 --> 00:11:58,620
Yeah.

333
00:11:58,620 --> 00:12:02,020
(Huang Jingyu)

334
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:11,620
(VIP seats in the front row
of the aquarium show)

335
00:12:11,660 --> 00:12:16,220
(Wang Anyu)

336
00:12:16,220 --> 00:12:17,140
(Hi)

337
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:22,660
(Fan Chengcheng filming)

338
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:24,020
(Hu Xianxu, Wang Anyu)
He's not moving forward.

339
00:12:32,380 --> 00:12:37,060
(Wang Anyu filming)

340
00:12:37,100 --> 00:12:39,900
(Wang Anyu, Hu Xianxu)

341
00:12:39,900 --> 00:12:40,420
(Huang Jingyu)

342
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:42,500
(This is even more like an aquarium now)

343
00:12:44,580 --> 00:12:45,500
(Hu Xianxu: You two)

344
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:46,580
(Just wait till we get back up there)

345
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:50,700
(Shen Teng, Hu Xianxu)

346
00:12:50,720 --> 00:12:51,340
Teng.

347
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:54,140
(Shen Teng)

348
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:55,340
(Hu Xianxu: Teng, don't be mad)

349
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:57,580
(Let's go for a walk on the ocean floor)

350
00:12:58,680 --> 00:12:59,320
Heading back!

351
00:13:02,140 --> 00:13:05,220
(Hu Xianxu)

352
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:12,140
(Hu Xianxu filming)

353
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:18,780
(Wang Churan filming)

354
00:13:23,680 --> 00:13:24,640
Let's swim back.

355
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:26,680
Need a ride?

356
00:13:28,460 --> 00:13:31,060
(Wang Anyu's Zhejiang spirit kicks in)

357
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:32,940
(Wang Anyu)

358
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:45,320
Refreshing.

359
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:47,800
I've never been down
to the ocean floor before.

360
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:48,680
Never in my life.

361
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:51,260
Jingyu was in there
looking just like a fish.

362
00:13:51,680 --> 00:13:52,720
Let's take a walk along the beach.

363
00:13:52,720 --> 00:13:53,480
Let's go.

364
00:13:54,880 --> 00:13:56,040
This scenery is so relaxing.

365
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:57,400
I'll always love the ocean breeze
and tropical islands.

366
00:13:57,400 --> 00:13:59,240
We should put that line on the postcard.

367
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:00,160
It'd make a great keepsake.

368
00:14:00,160 --> 00:14:02,000
Let's leave it to the amazing Taobao.

369
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,720
Search "Natural High" on Taobao

370
00:14:03,720 --> 00:14:05,960
to get a handwritten-style postcard
from our Sanya stop.

371
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:08,000
Plus, there's an 888-yuan travel fund.

372
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,160
You'll get something every day.

373
00:14:09,160 --> 00:14:10,560
We can do the postcard thing

374
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:11,520
at every stop.

375
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:12,880
Let's spread the joy

376
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:13,840
and hit the road together!

377
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:19,280
I've never seen this vehicle before.

378
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:38,320
Who's visiting Wuzhizhou Island
for the first time?

379
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,200
It's my first time here.

380
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,080
Same here.

381
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:42,680
It's everyone's first time.

382
00:14:42,680 --> 00:14:43,120
First time here.

383
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:44,080
I think I've been here before.

384
00:14:44,080 --> 00:14:44,960
You probably have.

385
00:14:45,400 --> 00:14:48,120
Have you guys ever been
to Monkey Island in Sanya?

386
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:49,320
Yeah.

387
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:51,400
Do the monkeys steal your stuff?

388
00:14:51,400 --> 00:14:53,120
One of them stole my bag once.

389
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:53,880
Really?

390
00:14:53,880 --> 00:14:54,080
Yeah.

391
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:55,120
And it still hasn't given it back?

392
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,440
Nope. It just took it.

393
00:14:57,080 --> 00:14:58,200
Was there anything valuable inside?

394
00:14:58,880 --> 00:14:59,320
No.

395
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:02,120
Well, even if there was,
there's nothing I could do.

396
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:03,400
I'm not exactly friends
with the monkeys.

397
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:08,680
Summer in Sanya

398
00:15:08,680 --> 00:15:10,280
is actually...

399
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:10,960
Cooler.

400
00:15:10,960 --> 00:15:11,960
Cooler than in a lot of other places.

401
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:14,040
We came to Sanya to escape the heat.

402
00:15:14,040 --> 00:15:14,800
I know right?

403
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:16,400
And the best part is,

404
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:18,080
it doesn't feel that humid and sticky.

405
00:15:18,960 --> 00:15:21,640
The breeze at night is pretty cool.

406
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:22,400
It's nice riding in those little carts.

407
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:26,960
Let's go.

408
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:27,840
Everybody off!

409
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:36,000
Hello, everyone!

410
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:37,120
Come on.

411
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:38,320
You just planted some coral.

412
00:15:38,320 --> 00:15:40,360
Now, let me show you a little cutie.

413
00:15:42,120 --> 00:15:43,000
Here's a question for everyone.

414
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,480
Is it an animal or a plant?

415
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:45,440
Or is it a microorganism?

416
00:15:45,720 --> 00:15:46,360
An animal.

417
00:15:47,040 --> 00:15:49,520
A microorganism.

418
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:52,960
Is it a sea hare?

419
00:15:53,640 --> 00:15:54,600
Not bad.

420
00:15:55,280 --> 00:15:56,200
Hu, you're impressive.

421
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:57,040
That's correct!

422
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:58,520
We've got a "biologist" here.

423
00:15:59,280 --> 00:16:00,240
Well, this

424
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:00,840
is an animal.

425
00:16:01,320 --> 00:16:02,260
(Chen Rui, PhD in Zoology, IOZ)
It has a lovely

426
00:16:02,260 --> 00:16:03,360
(CASE Secretary-General)
common name.

427
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:06,000
(Head of Shi Tan Ji Scientists Team)
Leaf sheep sea slug.

428
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:07,240
(Leaf sheep sea slug)
It's a type of mollusk.

429
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,520
It's also a sea hare.

430
00:16:08,520 --> 00:16:09,880
(Video sourced from the internet)
Back in 2000,

431
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:10,520
other scientists

432
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:12,400
used this group of sea slugs

433
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,560
as a biological model

434
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:14,280
to study

435
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:16,000
short-term and long-term memory.

436
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,480
Short-term memory
involves chemical changes,

437
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:18,880
while long-term memory
involves synapses.

438
00:16:18,880 --> 00:16:20,680
It also has one
of the most amazing abilities

439
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:22,160
of any creature on Earth.

440
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:24,520
It can feed on algae

441
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:26,000
and take the chloroplasts
from the algae,

442
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,880
(Kleptoplasty: Feeds on specific algae)
turning them into its own.

443
00:16:27,880 --> 00:16:29,200
(Keeps chloroplasts for photosynthesis)
Those green patches

444
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,720
(Eats more algae to replenish chloroplasts)
are actually chloroplasts.

445
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:32,640
It can then perform photosynthesis.

446
00:16:32,640 --> 00:16:34,480
(Materials sourced from the internet)
Earlier this year, Wuzhizhou Island

447
00:16:34,480 --> 00:16:36,600
recorded its first discovery
of this species.

448
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,920
This creature has extremely high

449
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:39,680
water quality requirements.

450
00:16:39,680 --> 00:16:40,760
Its presence

451
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:43,800
shows the ocean ecosystem is recovering.

452
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:45,040
The corals are slowly growing,

453
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:46,400
and leaf sheep are gradually appearing

454
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:47,560
among the coral reefs.

455
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:50,360
Now, for our next mission,

456
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:52,400
let's bring the wisdom
of slow-paced life

457
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:53,840
into the real world.

458
00:16:53,840 --> 00:16:55,920
This mission
is called "Slow-Moving Witnesses".

459
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:58,860
(Slow-Moving Witnesses)
Water is essential for marine life.

460
00:16:59,280 --> 00:17:00,680
Everyone needs to balance
a bowl of water on their head.

461
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:02,320
One of you

462
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:03,720
(Slow-Moving Witnesses)
will be the leaf sheep (wolf).

463
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:04,720
(1 leaf sheep & 7 algae)
The rest will be algae (good guys).

464
00:17:04,720 --> 00:17:05,520
(Algae)
The algae (good guys) must complete

465
00:17:05,520 --> 00:17:07,640
(Pufferfish, seahorse, sea snail, whale)
seven sea creature drawings.

466
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:09,600
(Stingray, dolphin, jellyfish, sea bream)
The leaf sheep (wolf)

467
00:17:09,600 --> 00:17:11,040
must use specific moves
to eliminate the algae (good guys).

468
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:12,600
After an elimination,
there's a 20-second cooldown

469
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:13,680
before attacking again.

470
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:15,080
(After an elimination)
The leaf sheep

471
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:16,400
(there's a 20-second cooldown)
can destroy the algae's drawings.

472
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:17,560
(Reporting location)
If anyone notices anything suspicious,

473
00:17:17,560 --> 00:17:19,520
they can "report" it
at the designated location.

474
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:22,400
(Drawing task locations)
There are eight drawing locations.

475
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:24,440
The algae (good guys) win
by completing all seven drawings.

476
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:26,040
(Slow-Moving Witnesses)
The leaf sheep (wolf) wins

477
00:17:26,040 --> 00:17:26,960
by eliminating
more than half of the players.

478
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:27,840
But there's one thing to remember.

479
00:17:27,840 --> 00:17:28,600
Throughout the game,

480
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:30,400
anyone who runs out of water
will be eliminated.

481
00:17:31,480 --> 00:17:33,480
What if my water runs out

482
00:17:33,480 --> 00:17:35,600
before he catches me?

483
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:37,080
Then you'll be eliminated.

484
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:38,200
We'll determine by checking if a tissue

485
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:40,020
can absorb water from your bowl.

486
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:41,420
(Water check: Can a tissue
absorb water from the bowl?)

487
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:41,800
Okay.

488
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:42,920
Let's go!

489
00:17:43,460 --> 00:17:44,740
(Assigning roles)

490
00:17:56,280 --> 00:17:58,320
Everyone, head to the spawn point.

491
00:18:09,460 --> 00:18:12,300
(Summer face wash)

492
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:17,620
(Shampoo edition)

493
00:18:17,640 --> 00:18:19,040
It's already spilling.

494
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:20,360
If we don't start soon,
it'll all spill out.

495
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:23,720
Wait, my bowl...

496
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:25,520
Is my bowl leaking?

497
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:30,100
(Nonstop flow)

498
00:18:30,120 --> 00:18:31,480
Is my bowl leaking?

499
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:39,320
I...

500
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:43,420
(Practically drowning)

501
00:18:44,560 --> 00:18:45,480
My bowl isn't leaking?

502
00:18:45,480 --> 00:18:46,280
Are you sure?

503
00:18:48,200 --> 00:18:49,040
Let's start! Hurry!

504
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:50,720
I'm gonna drown if we don't start!

505
00:18:53,220 --> 00:18:55,740
(Slow-motion witness officially begins)

506
00:18:55,820 --> 00:18:58,780
(Moving in slow motion)

507
00:18:58,780 --> 00:19:05,140
(Leaf sheep (wolf), confidential)

508
00:19:05,160 --> 00:19:06,200
I'm scared to even laugh now.

509
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:13,080
Bing!

510
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:14,200
Yours...

511
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:20,680
No way.

512
00:19:20,680 --> 00:19:22,280
I can't even walk like this.

513
00:19:25,420 --> 00:19:28,620
(Automatic faucet)

514
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:33,220
(Can't take a single step)

515
00:19:33,300 --> 00:19:37,820
(Everyone's forced
to move at a snail's pace)

516
00:19:37,840 --> 00:19:39,720
Hurry and find somewhere to draw!

517
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:41,680
Yeah, I'm scared to go out there.

518
00:19:41,680 --> 00:19:42,180
Why?

519
00:19:42,460 --> 00:19:43,580
(Extra cautious)

520
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:44,440
Where is everyone?

521
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:46,160
Trust me. I'm a good guy.

522
00:19:51,580 --> 00:19:53,180
(Task spot found)

523
00:19:55,020 --> 00:19:56,780
(Algae (good guys) tasks: 1/7)

524
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:58,120
Let me check this out.

525
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:00,520
Jellyfish.

526
00:20:04,040 --> 00:20:04,480
Here.

527
00:20:05,540 --> 00:20:06,700
(Algae (good guys) tasks: 2/7)

528
00:20:06,720 --> 00:20:07,320
Done.

529
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:10,400
Are you done?

530
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:10,880
I'm done.

531
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,480
Let me see if you're good or...

532
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:13,760
(Checking identity)
Of course I'm a good guy.

533
00:20:13,760 --> 00:20:15,280
My drawing's amazing.

534
00:20:15,280 --> 00:20:17,920
Just look at this jellyfish landscape.

535
00:20:17,920 --> 00:20:19,720
(No identity check. Instantly convinced)
Isn't it beautiful?

536
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:20,720
Are you serious?

537
00:20:22,780 --> 00:20:24,100
(No sudden stops)

538
00:20:24,120 --> 00:20:24,920
How much is left?

539
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:26,120
What are you doing?

540
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:27,200
How much is left?

541
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:28,120
Whose?

542
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:29,520
How much do I have left?

543
00:20:29,520 --> 00:20:30,000
Yours is full.

544
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,760
You scared me
into spilling half of it.

545
00:20:33,880 --> 00:20:34,800
What's wrong with you?

546
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:35,480
No...

547
00:20:35,480 --> 00:20:36,320
Why'd you suddenly...

548
00:20:36,320 --> 00:20:38,600
No, it suddenly started pouring out!

549
00:20:39,920 --> 00:20:41,160
Is this a task spot?

550
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:42,960
Is it?

551
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:44,160
Pufferfish.

552
00:20:46,780 --> 00:20:49,260
(Algae (good guys) tasks: 3/7)

553
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:52,560
I'm done drawing.

554
00:20:52,560 --> 00:20:53,420
(Keeping watch)

555
00:20:55,920 --> 00:20:57,000
Let's vouch for each other.

556
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:58,700
(Algae (good guys) verify each other)
Let's stick together.

557
00:20:58,720 --> 00:20:59,440
Bai,

558
00:20:59,440 --> 00:20:59,920
let's go.

559
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:00,840
Let's stick together.

560
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:03,080
If we go together,

561
00:21:03,080 --> 00:21:04,300
(Then again)
we might both get eliminated.

562
00:21:04,340 --> 00:21:05,900
(Doubting each other's abilities)

563
00:21:06,080 --> 00:21:08,200
I can't keep my head steady at all.

564
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:09,600
What did you do to end up like that?

565
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:11,880
How'd you get so soaked?

566
00:21:11,880 --> 00:21:12,480
Is there anything here?

567
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,280
There's a task spot here.

568
00:21:13,280 --> 00:21:13,800
It's done.

569
00:21:13,800 --> 00:21:14,320
All done?

570
00:21:14,320 --> 00:21:14,680
Let's find another spot.

571
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:15,300
Let's go.

572
00:21:15,300 --> 00:21:16,180
(Finally crawled all the way here)

573
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:21,000
Go on, you.

574
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:23,040
Just go.

575
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:25,840
This is my drawing. Go.

576
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:28,880
What are you doing?

577
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:29,200
Don't move.

578
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:30,320
Then go back and draw first.

579
00:21:32,640 --> 00:21:33,360
Go back and draw first.

580
00:21:33,360 --> 00:21:33,920
(Suspicious)
Something's off about him.

581
00:21:33,920 --> 00:21:34,680
Wait till I'm out before you come out.

582
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:36,120
He's suspicious.

583
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:38,260
(Getting out of there first)

584
00:21:38,360 --> 00:21:40,120
You two have me trapped here.

585
00:21:41,980 --> 00:21:42,780
(Watching closely)

586
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:43,320
Don't move.

587
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:49,800
Oh no! I spilled it!

588
00:21:49,800 --> 00:21:51,400
You spilled it yourself!

589
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:52,520
Don't...

590
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:53,720
How much is left?

591
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:54,720
Half.

592
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:56,440
It's fine. You can spill a little more.

593
00:22:00,100 --> 00:22:02,260
(Crawling off
to find another drawing spot)

594
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:06,160
Mr. Huang,
have you drawn yet? Mr. Huang?

595
00:22:06,160 --> 00:22:07,360
I haven't even found a spot!

596
00:22:09,100 --> 00:22:10,780
(Task already completed)

597
00:22:13,980 --> 00:22:16,500
(Searching everywhere
for a drawing spot)

598
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:24,200
I'm done.

599
00:22:25,240 --> 00:22:26,160
I'm done.

600
00:22:27,560 --> 00:22:28,600
Dude, you're really selling it.

601
00:22:28,600 --> 00:22:30,040
(Suspect identified)
You're really selling it.

602
00:22:30,040 --> 00:22:31,440
I'm not.

603
00:22:42,740 --> 00:22:44,540
(Algae (good guys) tasks: 4/7)

604
00:22:44,540 --> 00:22:46,340
(Algae (good guys)
have three drawings left)

605
00:22:48,940 --> 00:22:51,500
(Sneaking closer)

606
00:22:55,680 --> 00:22:57,320
You're probably a Werewolf, right?

607
00:22:57,320 --> 00:22:58,340
(Suspicious character)
Something's off about you.

608
00:22:58,350 --> 00:22:59,640
You're out of water.

609
00:22:59,640 --> 00:23:01,180
(Still has some left)
I've finished all my drawings.

610
00:23:01,260 --> 00:23:02,660
(Keeping his distance)

611
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:05,880
Can I draw at the same spot again?

612
00:23:05,880 --> 00:23:07,320
Of course not.

613
00:23:07,320 --> 00:23:08,560
(Each task spot can only be used once)
So I can't?

614
00:23:08,560 --> 00:23:09,320
Yeah.

615
00:23:09,320 --> 00:23:10,920
Then I came here for nothing.

616
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:17,660
(Sudden appearance)

617
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,320
Nobody come near me.

618
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:24,320
Stay away.

619
00:23:34,300 --> 00:23:35,700
(Wang Churan's POV)

620
00:23:35,740 --> 00:23:37,220
(Task spot found)

621
00:23:37,260 --> 00:23:40,140
(Algae (good guys) tasks: 5/7)

622
00:23:40,180 --> 00:23:40,900
(Staring)

623
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:41,760
I'm done drawing.

624
00:23:54,460 --> 00:23:56,900
(Back again)

625
00:24:00,440 --> 00:24:01,080
She's

626
00:24:01,080 --> 00:24:02,320
sneaking around and shaking.

627
00:24:02,320 --> 00:24:03,360
What are you doing?

628
00:24:04,500 --> 00:24:05,980
(Seen but ignored)

629
00:24:07,320 --> 00:24:07,880
Churan!

630
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:11,720
We're on the same team!

631
00:24:15,840 --> 00:24:17,320
You're acting way too shady.

632
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:20,920
Where do I find a drawing?

633
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:22,800
Can you stay away from me?

634
00:24:23,040 --> 00:24:23,800
I haven't found one.

635
00:24:29,080 --> 00:24:30,920
There's a drawing in that bathroom.

636
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:32,000
(Revealing she's algae (good guy))
There's one in that bathroom.

637
00:24:47,340 --> 00:24:49,860
(Hu's drawing)

638
00:24:53,660 --> 00:24:54,940
(Drawing over it)

639
00:24:57,220 --> 00:25:00,420
(Busy hands)

640
00:25:01,200 --> 00:25:01,960
What's she doing?

641
00:25:03,160 --> 00:25:03,880
Someone's here.

642
00:25:04,840 --> 00:25:06,320
She's ruining the drawing, right?

643
00:25:06,580 --> 00:25:08,500
(Quickly pulling her hand back)

644
00:25:10,200 --> 00:25:11,680
She's ruining the drawing, right?

645
00:25:13,060 --> 00:25:14,900
(What's going on here?)

646
00:25:15,120 --> 00:25:15,960
She's ruining it.

647
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:17,640
Sound the alarm!

648
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:19,480
- Why?
- Sound the alarm!

649
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:19,960
I drew another one.

650
00:25:19,960 --> 00:25:21,080
Sound the alarm! She's ruining it!

651
00:25:21,080 --> 00:25:21,960
(That's definitely leaf sheep (wolf))
I drew one!

652
00:25:21,960 --> 00:25:22,920
No, I already drew there!

653
00:25:22,920 --> 00:25:23,600
Then why'd you draw again?

654
00:25:23,600 --> 00:25:24,600
Sound the alarm! Hurry!

655
00:25:24,600 --> 00:25:25,080
How?

656
00:25:25,080 --> 00:25:25,760
Sound the alarm!

657
00:25:25,960 --> 00:25:26,680
Sound the alarm!

658
00:25:27,320 --> 00:25:31,000
Sound the alarm!

659
00:25:32,120 --> 00:25:33,320
I can't believe this!

660
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:34,680
Someone's sounding the alarm!

661
00:25:35,320 --> 00:25:36,560
What happened?

662
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:39,000
Sound the alarm!

663
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:40,560
Was it Churan?

664
00:25:40,560 --> 00:25:40,890
Churan.

665
00:25:40,890 --> 00:25:41,240
Sound the alarm?

666
00:25:41,240 --> 00:25:42,440
All of us in these palaces

667
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:43,440
have to go over there.

668
00:25:45,040 --> 00:25:47,360
They're like the Calabash Brothers!

669
00:25:49,320 --> 00:25:50,560
I have a suspect!

670
00:25:50,620 --> 00:25:52,380
(Underwater villagers sound the alarm)

671
00:25:52,400 --> 00:25:53,120
Wait.

672
00:25:53,120 --> 00:25:53,600
Hold on.

673
00:25:53,600 --> 00:25:54,520
Did I get the rules wrong?

674
00:25:54,520 --> 00:25:55,200
Like, say

675
00:25:55,200 --> 00:25:56,160
if someone's drawn here,

676
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:57,400
you can't draw again, right?

677
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:58,320
Yeah. Only one drawing.

678
00:25:58,840 --> 00:25:59,400
I didn't know.

679
00:25:59,400 --> 00:26:00,880
I just drew another one.

680
00:26:00,880 --> 00:26:02,080
Come on.

681
00:26:02,080 --> 00:26:02,640
Let's discuss.

682
00:26:03,240 --> 00:26:03,880
Wang Churan,

683
00:26:03,880 --> 00:26:04,800
(Leaf sheep (wolf), the suspect)
found her.

684
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:07,000
I have to defend myself this time.

685
00:26:07,300 --> 00:26:08,480
(Underwater meeting, round 1)
Listen, guys.

686
00:26:08,480 --> 00:26:09,480
If I wanted to ruin it,

687
00:26:09,480 --> 00:26:10,080
then earlier,

688
00:26:10,080 --> 00:26:10,840
shouldn't I have

689
00:26:10,840 --> 00:26:11,960
ruined his drawing right away?

690
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:12,680
But I didn't.

691
00:26:12,680 --> 00:26:13,960
(Claims she misunderstood the rules)
I just misunderstood the rules.

692
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:15,160
So I drew another one,

693
00:26:15,160 --> 00:26:15,680
right?

694
00:26:15,680 --> 00:26:16,640
- But yours...
- Go check for yourselves.

695
00:26:16,640 --> 00:26:17,440
It's not ruined.

696
00:26:17,440 --> 00:26:18,840
But you were acting really suspicious.

697
00:26:18,840 --> 00:26:20,640
You kept sneaking around

698
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:21,760
and looking everywhere.

699
00:26:21,760 --> 00:26:22,560
Seriously.

700
00:26:22,560 --> 00:26:24,040
And when we came in,

701
00:26:24,040 --> 00:26:25,360
you hid behind the door!

702
00:26:25,360 --> 00:26:26,720
(Anyone would find that suspicious)
No, I was scared!

703
00:26:26,720 --> 00:26:28,280
Why hide if you're innocent?

704
00:26:28,280 --> 00:26:29,920
You were acting pretty shady.

705
00:26:29,920 --> 00:26:32,160
I was scared a bad guy would come in!

706
00:26:32,680 --> 00:26:33,480
A bad guy?

707
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:34,440
If a bad guy came in, I'd hide

708
00:26:34,440 --> 00:26:37,000
so I could see who it was!

709
00:26:37,320 --> 00:26:39,480
Then why'd you draw there again?

710
00:26:39,480 --> 00:26:40,520
He'd already finished.

711
00:26:40,520 --> 00:26:41,200
No, wait.

712
00:26:41,200 --> 00:26:42,200
I went in to find Hu.

713
00:26:42,200 --> 00:26:43,480
Guess what we both saw?

714
00:26:44,720 --> 00:26:45,320
We saw

715
00:26:45,320 --> 00:26:47,080
a hand sticking out

716
00:26:47,080 --> 00:26:49,120
from behind the bathroom door, drawing!

717
00:26:49,180 --> 00:26:52,260
(Incident replay)

718
00:26:52,640 --> 00:26:54,320
Then Hu yelled, "What are you doing?"

719
00:26:54,320 --> 00:26:55,360
And the hand disappeared.

720
00:26:55,680 --> 00:26:57,240
So I said I'd catch whoever it was.

721
00:26:57,760 --> 00:26:58,880
I reached the door. Nobody was there.

722
00:26:59,240 --> 00:26:59,680
Then

723
00:27:00,120 --> 00:27:01,400
I went farther in and found

724
00:27:02,040 --> 00:27:02,720
Wang Churan behind the door.

725
00:27:03,400 --> 00:27:04,720
She said she was finishing the drawing.

726
00:27:04,880 --> 00:27:06,360
As for that drawing,

727
00:27:06,360 --> 00:27:07,840
I don't know how much she completed.

728
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:09,480
No need to question that.

729
00:27:09,480 --> 00:27:10,440
I finished that drawing.

730
00:27:10,440 --> 00:27:11,860
(The conch drawing's creator)

731
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:13,800
Was he drawing a snake?

732
00:27:15,280 --> 00:27:16,600
She went and added legs to it.

733
00:27:19,320 --> 00:27:20,480
See? Once I went in,

734
00:27:20,480 --> 00:27:22,480
destroying it on the spot would've been

735
00:27:22,480 --> 00:27:23,360
the quickest and smartest move.

736
00:27:23,760 --> 00:27:24,200
But I didn't.

737
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:25,200
But I was right next to you.

738
00:27:25,200 --> 00:27:25,920
You couldn't destroy it
with both of them there.

739
00:27:25,920 --> 00:27:26,800
They were both in there.

740
00:27:26,800 --> 00:27:27,880
No, he'd already left.

741
00:27:28,120 --> 00:27:29,920
No, I think you were planning

742
00:27:30,240 --> 00:27:32,320
to pretend you were drawing.

743
00:27:32,320 --> 00:27:34,600
Then once we left,

744
00:27:34,600 --> 00:27:35,840
you'd tear up the drawing.

745
00:27:35,840 --> 00:27:37,040
I think

746
00:27:37,040 --> 00:27:38,400
we should vote Churan out first.

747
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:39,240
Take one for the team.

748
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:40,540
It's because I'm not a bad guy,

749
00:27:40,540 --> 00:27:41,660
(Desperately defending herself)
so I had no reason to draw over it.

750
00:27:41,660 --> 00:27:42,600
Either way,

751
00:27:42,600 --> 00:27:43,800
you're taking the fall this round.

752
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:49,680
I think Hu's been

753
00:27:49,680 --> 00:27:50,640
really suspicious this round.

754
00:27:51,040 --> 00:27:51,320
Fine.

755
00:27:51,320 --> 00:27:52,880
If you're innocent,

756
00:27:52,880 --> 00:27:54,160
I'll take the fall next round.

757
00:27:55,960 --> 00:27:57,160
No need. I will.

758
00:27:57,160 --> 00:27:57,760
How about this?

759
00:27:58,760 --> 00:28:00,200
Let's eliminate one of you two first.

760
00:28:00,200 --> 00:28:00,980
(Might as well eliminate both)

761
00:28:05,800 --> 00:28:08,160
Now you even wanna eliminate
whoever sounded the alarm!

762
00:28:08,720 --> 00:28:09,280
How about this?

763
00:28:09,280 --> 00:28:09,720
Here.

764
00:28:11,240 --> 00:28:12,680
Anyu's out this round.

765
00:28:13,960 --> 00:28:14,840
Anyu's out.

766
00:28:20,700 --> 00:28:22,260
(Things have taken
a hilariously bad turn)

767
00:28:23,600 --> 00:28:25,640
He hasn't said a word.
That's suspicious!

768
00:28:25,640 --> 00:28:26,000
I...

769
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:27,480
(Joining the pile-on)
Very suspicious, Anyu!

770
00:28:27,480 --> 00:28:29,080
Last season,

771
00:28:29,080 --> 00:28:30,400
in the very first episode,

772
00:28:30,400 --> 00:28:32,960
I was probably a little too outspoken.

773
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:35,080
Everyone kept voting me out first.

774
00:28:35,080 --> 00:28:35,880
So I got smarter.

775
00:28:35,880 --> 00:28:36,880
I decided to stay quiet.

776
00:28:37,800 --> 00:28:38,440
And it's still me!

777
00:28:38,440 --> 00:28:39,360
Why'd you stay quiet?

778
00:28:39,360 --> 00:28:40,800
You call that getting smarter?

779
00:28:40,800 --> 00:28:42,720
You just went to the other extreme.

780
00:28:43,560 --> 00:28:45,800
The loudest and the quietest.

781
00:28:45,800 --> 00:28:46,800
Then let me say something.

782
00:28:46,800 --> 00:28:48,040
Go ahead.

783
00:28:48,040 --> 00:28:49,440
Say a few words before you go.

784
00:28:51,440 --> 00:28:52,880
I think Churan...

785
00:28:52,880 --> 00:28:53,840
I have a point, right?

786
00:28:53,840 --> 00:28:54,200
No.

787
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:55,280
From what I know

788
00:28:55,280 --> 00:28:55,960
about you...

789
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:57,680
We only met yesterday.

790
00:28:57,680 --> 00:28:58,720
Based on what I know...

791
00:28:58,720 --> 00:29:00,360
Based on knowing you for a day.

792
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:02,000
Yeah. From our first day together,

793
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:02,840
I think

794
00:29:03,160 --> 00:29:03,880
she's innocent.

795
00:29:03,940 --> 00:29:04,680
(What a genius)

796
00:29:04,680 --> 00:29:05,720
I think

797
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:07,600
her defense

798
00:29:07,600 --> 00:29:09,320
didn't make much sense.

799
00:29:09,320 --> 00:29:10,600
But

800
00:29:10,600 --> 00:29:11,840
her eyes looked sincere.

801
00:29:13,120 --> 00:29:14,720
Look how sincere my eyes are now.

802
00:29:15,120 --> 00:29:17,520
And the first person
I saw when I spawned

803
00:29:17,520 --> 00:29:18,800
was Churan.

804
00:29:19,080 --> 00:29:20,520
The first person you saw

805
00:29:20,520 --> 00:29:21,760
when you spawned was Churan?

806
00:29:22,440 --> 00:29:22,840
Yeah.

807
00:29:23,160 --> 00:29:24,280
You two...

808
00:29:25,240 --> 00:29:26,480
You don't even look alike.

809
00:29:29,080 --> 00:29:32,640
Right. I was at my spawn point.

810
00:29:33,080 --> 00:29:33,840
Right.

811
00:29:34,360 --> 00:29:36,000
I think it's Teng.

812
00:29:36,280 --> 00:29:37,120
(Leaf sheep (wolf) suspect list)
What?

813
00:29:37,120 --> 00:29:37,940
(Wang Churan, Wang Anyu, Shen Teng)

814
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:43,280
I still haven't even found

815
00:29:43,280 --> 00:29:44,320
my second task spot!

816
00:29:44,320 --> 00:29:45,840
Look how long it's been!

817
00:29:45,840 --> 00:29:47,360
Now everyone's arguing!

818
00:29:47,640 --> 00:29:49,280
Teng hasn't finished a single drawing.

819
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:51,280
I'm soaked and still haven't
found my second one!

820
00:29:51,280 --> 00:29:52,240
Well, if you put it that way,

821
00:29:52,240 --> 00:29:53,680
I think he

822
00:29:53,680 --> 00:29:56,160
kept creeping along

823
00:29:56,160 --> 00:29:57,440
trying to get close to me.

824
00:29:57,440 --> 00:29:59,600
That's even more suspicious.

825
00:29:59,600 --> 00:30:00,400
Exactly.

826
00:30:02,140 --> 00:30:04,380
(Let me think)

827
00:30:05,320 --> 00:30:06,320
Bai.

828
00:30:06,320 --> 00:30:07,180
Let's vote Bai this round.

829
00:30:07,260 --> 00:30:08,500
(Accusations flying everywhere)

830
00:30:08,500 --> 00:30:09,900
(Leaf sheep (wolf) suspect list: Wang Churan,
Wang Anyu, Shen Teng, Bai Jingting)

831
00:30:11,640 --> 00:30:12,840
No, I finished mine.

832
00:30:13,200 --> 00:30:14,320
I drew the pufferfish.

833
00:30:14,600 --> 00:30:17,200
Bai and I can vouch for each other.

834
00:30:17,480 --> 00:30:18,360
What's with you two?

835
00:30:18,360 --> 00:30:19,800
Vouching for each other?

836
00:30:19,800 --> 00:30:21,960
We both watched each other

837
00:30:21,960 --> 00:30:23,600
(Each other's eyewitnesses)
finish a drawing properly.

838
00:30:23,600 --> 00:30:24,560
You were close together?

839
00:30:24,560 --> 00:30:25,440
Yeah, we were.

840
00:30:25,440 --> 00:30:26,640
Then you had no choice but to draw.

841
00:30:27,040 --> 00:30:27,720
Yeah, no...

842
00:30:27,720 --> 00:30:28,840
You had to draw.

843
00:30:29,960 --> 00:30:31,200
I finished mine first.

844
00:30:31,200 --> 00:30:33,920
Then Mr. Huang showed up.

845
00:30:34,180 --> 00:30:35,320
I didn't even go in.

846
00:30:35,320 --> 00:30:35,960
Right, he didn't.

847
00:30:35,960 --> 00:30:36,680
I said I'd finished.

848
00:30:36,680 --> 00:30:37,240
He'd finished too.

849
00:30:37,240 --> 00:30:38,680
Then the three of us left.

850
00:30:40,680 --> 00:30:42,100
Well, speaking of Mr. Huang...

851
00:30:42,100 --> 00:30:42,440
(Leaf sheep (wolf) suspect list:)

852
00:30:42,440 --> 00:30:43,080
(Wang Churan, Wang Anyu, Shen Teng,
Bai Jingting, Huang Jingyu)

853
00:30:43,080 --> 00:30:43,960
(More wild accusations)
Why does Mr. Huang keep going

854
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:45,480
to such remote spots?

855
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:47,800
And he's been moving all over the place.

856
00:30:47,800 --> 00:30:48,320
Right?

857
00:30:48,320 --> 00:30:49,800
He'd already moved from that room

858
00:30:49,800 --> 00:30:51,120
to here when he called for the alarm.

859
00:30:52,960 --> 00:30:54,640
(Taking turns accusing everyone)
So we're targeting whoever's quiet now?

860
00:30:54,920 --> 00:30:55,600
Well, in that case...

861
00:30:55,600 --> 00:30:56,120
Bing!

862
00:30:56,120 --> 00:30:57,120
- I think it's Bing!
- If that's how we're playing...

863
00:30:57,380 --> 00:30:57,960
(Accusations flying even wilder)

864
00:30:57,960 --> 00:30:59,560
Then it must be Bing!

865
00:31:02,320 --> 00:31:02,960
I did draw something.

866
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:04,000
You might not have seen it,

867
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:05,080
but I left my handwriting.

868
00:31:06,200 --> 00:31:07,280
Whoever touches it is a dog.

869
00:31:07,620 --> 00:31:11,460
(Whoever touches it is a dog)

870
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:13,320
That's just...

871
00:31:13,320 --> 00:31:15,160
That's so mean!

872
00:31:15,180 --> 00:31:16,700
(Personal watermark)

873
00:31:16,800 --> 00:31:18,400
No, I actually think

874
00:31:18,400 --> 00:31:19,800
Jingyu's the most suspicious!

875
00:31:20,200 --> 00:31:21,320
He sounded the alarm

876
00:31:21,760 --> 00:31:23,600
to get a good guy eliminated.

877
00:31:24,560 --> 00:31:25,040
I...

878
00:31:25,040 --> 00:31:26,600
Everyone was caught up in the moment!

879
00:31:26,600 --> 00:31:27,600
They were all yelling,
"Sound the alarm!"

880
00:31:27,600 --> 00:31:29,520
I just got here first!

881
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:29,920
No.

882
00:31:29,920 --> 00:31:31,000
Who yelled it first?

883
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:31,840
Everyone was yelling it!

884
00:31:31,840 --> 00:31:32,680
No.

885
00:31:32,680 --> 00:31:34,280
He says everyone was yelling.
We need to take him out.

886
00:31:34,280 --> 00:31:34,840
Right?

887
00:31:34,840 --> 00:31:35,320
Only Jingyu was yelling.

888
00:31:35,320 --> 00:31:36,040
Did you yell?

889
00:31:36,560 --> 00:31:36,840
I said

890
00:31:36,840 --> 00:31:37,660
we could do it.

891
00:31:37,840 --> 00:31:39,400
I said it was a good idea.

892
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:40,840
Did Fan Chengcheng yell?

893
00:31:41,200 --> 00:31:42,880
I only said I was considering it.

894
00:31:42,880 --> 00:31:44,400
But you're the one who did it.

895
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:47,600
That's just stirring things up!

896
00:31:47,600 --> 00:31:48,240
I yelled too!

897
00:31:50,320 --> 00:31:50,840
I yelled too.

898
00:31:53,040 --> 00:31:53,840
Then let's eliminate Jingyu.

899
00:31:53,840 --> 00:31:54,880
There's no one else.

900
00:31:55,320 --> 00:31:56,400
You all yelled it!

901
00:31:56,400 --> 00:31:57,400
I sound the alarm and get eliminated?

902
00:31:57,400 --> 00:31:58,000
Can't be helped.

903
00:31:58,000 --> 00:31:58,880
You're just too helpful.

904
00:32:02,600 --> 00:32:03,720
No. Society can't work like that.

905
00:32:03,720 --> 00:32:05,920
Right. We should encourage
helping others.

906
00:32:05,920 --> 00:32:07,840
We can't punish someone for helping!

907
00:32:07,840 --> 00:32:08,720
That's not right!

908
00:32:08,720 --> 00:32:10,740
(Good people still exist)

909
00:32:11,080 --> 00:32:12,600
Who hasn't drawn anything yet?

910
00:32:12,600 --> 00:32:13,640
I haven't.

911
00:32:13,640 --> 00:32:14,280
Two.

912
00:32:14,560 --> 00:32:15,880
Churan hasn't drawn, right?

913
00:32:15,880 --> 00:32:17,440
I did. I drew the same thing.

914
00:32:17,440 --> 00:32:19,480
Then that doesn't count.

915
00:32:19,480 --> 00:32:22,840
We should vote out someone
who hasn't drawn.

916
00:32:24,960 --> 00:32:26,320
Stop bringing up the drawings.

917
00:32:26,320 --> 00:32:27,800
You think I didn't wanna draw?

918
00:32:27,800 --> 00:32:29,000
They'd all been done!

919
00:32:29,000 --> 00:32:29,760
Then it's you.

920
00:32:30,680 --> 00:32:32,080
You're attacking everyone now?

921
00:32:32,080 --> 00:32:33,200
Get him out first!

922
00:32:33,200 --> 00:32:34,440
I'm definitely innocent.

923
00:32:34,440 --> 00:32:35,360
I'm the goodest guy here.

924
00:32:35,360 --> 00:32:36,560
I've done the most good.

925
00:32:37,680 --> 00:32:39,040
Let's vote.

926
00:32:39,560 --> 00:32:40,000
I...

927
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:40,980
(No clues.
What are they even analyzing?)

928
00:32:42,680 --> 00:32:44,120
It's really not that serious.

929
00:32:48,880 --> 00:32:51,680
I don't think Anyu
or Jingyu is the wolf.

930
00:32:51,680 --> 00:32:52,600
Because at the start,

931
00:32:52,600 --> 00:32:53,800
I saw them both right away.

932
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:54,880
Then you're the one leaving.

933
00:32:54,940 --> 00:32:56,500
(How are we back to square one?)

934
00:32:59,320 --> 00:33:01,040
Churan, just tell us.

935
00:33:01,040 --> 00:33:02,160
Can you take the fall?

936
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:03,480
Will you take one for the team?

937
00:33:03,480 --> 00:33:04,240
If you all vote for me,

938
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:05,160
I'm fine with it.

939
00:33:05,160 --> 00:33:06,080
But I won't volunteer.

940
00:33:06,080 --> 00:33:06,480
(You're okay with it)

941
00:33:06,480 --> 00:33:06,800
Okay.

942
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:09,640
You're okay with it.

943
00:33:09,640 --> 00:33:11,000
That's all we need.

944
00:33:11,400 --> 00:33:12,840
Nice look.

945
00:33:13,600 --> 00:33:13,960
Okay.

946
00:33:13,960 --> 00:33:14,760
Come on, let's vote!

947
00:33:14,760 --> 00:33:17,100
Three, two, one.

948
00:33:17,500 --> 00:33:18,820
(Shen Teng x2, Wang Churan x3,
Hu Xianxu x1, abstentions x2)

949
00:33:18,840 --> 00:33:19,680
What about the votes in the back?

950
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:21,800
We really have no idea.

951
00:33:21,800 --> 00:33:24,040
Neither of us saw anything!

952
00:33:24,720 --> 00:33:26,100
Okay, Churan's eliminated.

953
00:33:26,100 --> 00:33:27,260
(Wang Churan out)

954
00:33:27,640 --> 00:33:28,720
The game...

955
00:33:29,840 --> 00:33:30,320
continues.

956
00:33:36,080 --> 00:33:36,440
Oh no.

957
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:38,720
She really was innocent. We're screwed.

958
00:33:39,400 --> 00:33:41,120
Okay, everyone,
return to your spawn points.

959
00:33:41,120 --> 00:33:41,960
The game continues.

960
00:33:42,560 --> 00:33:43,640
I'm gonna find out who it is!

961
00:33:43,840 --> 00:33:45,280
Sorry, Churan.

962
00:33:45,280 --> 00:33:46,720
I wrongly accused you.

963
00:33:46,720 --> 00:33:48,080
Churan, I never doubted you.

964
00:33:48,460 --> 00:33:49,860
(Yeah, right)

965
00:34:05,560 --> 00:34:07,480
I think whoever sounded
the alarm is suspicious.

966
00:34:07,480 --> 00:34:10,160
(Suspecting Mr. Huang)
He knew nobody suspected him.

967
00:34:10,160 --> 00:34:11,240
So he sounded the alarm.

968
00:34:11,240 --> 00:34:12,480
If the alarm worked,

969
00:34:12,480 --> 00:34:13,600
we'd lose another good guy.

970
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:15,520
I'm keeping my eyes glued
to this drawing.

971
00:34:16,780 --> 00:34:18,940
(Slow-motion witness, round 2 begins)

972
00:34:18,940 --> 00:34:20,480
(Leaf sheep (wolf), confidential)

973
00:34:20,480 --> 00:34:22,240
Where's Jingyu's spawn point?

974
00:34:22,880 --> 00:34:23,480
No idea.

975
00:34:23,480 --> 00:34:24,480
I'll keep watch here.

976
00:34:24,480 --> 00:34:25,560
You go somewhere else.

977
00:34:25,560 --> 00:34:26,600
I'm staying here.

978
00:34:26,600 --> 00:34:28,040
I seriously suspect Jingyu.

979
00:34:28,640 --> 00:34:29,120
Okay.

980
00:34:30,120 --> 00:34:31,500
I'll check Jingyu's spot.

981
00:34:31,500 --> 00:34:32,060
(Suspect locked in)

982
00:34:32,600 --> 00:34:33,380
Bai!

983
00:34:33,380 --> 00:34:34,740
(Looking for fellow algae)

984
00:34:34,760 --> 00:34:35,800
Let's meet up first.

985
00:34:36,680 --> 00:34:38,440
(Top leaf sheep (wolf) suspect)
I'm with Huang Jingyu.

986
00:34:38,440 --> 00:34:39,400
I can see him.

987
00:34:41,320 --> 00:34:42,200
Where are you going?

988
00:34:42,200 --> 00:34:43,320
To the bathroom.

989
00:34:43,320 --> 00:34:44,040
The bathroom?

990
00:34:45,440 --> 00:34:47,040
He needs to use the bathroom now.

991
00:34:47,040 --> 00:34:49,040
(Following him)
Then I'd better watch my drawing.

992
00:34:49,600 --> 00:34:50,400
Bai!

993
00:34:50,400 --> 00:34:50,920
Coming.

994
00:34:50,920 --> 00:34:52,960
With all three of us here,
he can't strike.

995
00:34:52,960 --> 00:34:53,240
Yeah.

996
00:34:54,760 --> 00:34:56,360
That bathroom's see-through.

997
00:34:56,360 --> 00:34:57,840
You really need to go?

998
00:34:57,840 --> 00:34:59,120
I really do.

999
00:34:59,780 --> 00:35:01,780
(Searching for a bathroom)

1000
00:35:01,780 --> 00:35:04,820
(Following closely)

1001
00:35:05,640 --> 00:35:06,560
Is this one see-through?

1002
00:35:06,560 --> 00:35:08,120
Is this bathroom see-through?

1003
00:35:10,160 --> 00:35:11,120
This one's good.

1004
00:35:11,960 --> 00:35:12,480
This'll work.

1005
00:35:13,140 --> 00:35:19,460
(Listening in)

1006
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:23,640
He's actually peeing.

1007
00:35:23,900 --> 00:35:25,980
(Hahaha)

1008
00:35:31,600 --> 00:35:33,640
We should secretly watch from here

1009
00:35:33,640 --> 00:35:35,720
to see if Mr. Huang ruins that drawing.

1010
00:35:35,720 --> 00:35:38,380
See if he starts
asking around afterward.

1011
00:35:38,420 --> 00:35:41,220
(The world's most obvious spies)

1012
00:35:41,560 --> 00:35:42,240
Those two...

1013
00:35:43,820 --> 00:35:44,620
(Dumb and dumber)

1014
00:35:44,640 --> 00:35:46,440
Are they seriously watching that openly?

1015
00:35:50,980 --> 00:35:54,100
(Keeping watch)

1016
00:35:56,160 --> 00:35:57,120
I can't see clearly!

1017
00:35:57,740 --> 00:35:59,660
(Is he drawing or destroying it?)

1018
00:35:59,680 --> 00:36:00,520
Is he drawing?

1019
00:36:00,520 --> 00:36:01,920
Nobody's drawn here yet?

1020
00:36:09,880 --> 00:36:10,880
Mahua FunAge.

1021
00:36:11,880 --> 00:36:13,500
That's their movie logo!

1022
00:36:13,500 --> 00:36:15,780
(Mahua FunAge)

1023
00:36:21,480 --> 00:36:22,040
Who's there?

1024
00:36:23,240 --> 00:36:24,360
Why'd someone make a noise?

1025
00:36:24,820 --> 00:36:29,220
(Face-to-face horror movie)

1026
00:36:29,240 --> 00:36:30,200
Should I sound the alarm?

1027
00:36:31,680 --> 00:36:34,440
I just came to see
if you'd drawn anything.

1028
00:36:36,840 --> 00:36:38,560
You scared me!

1029
00:36:39,320 --> 00:36:41,560
That shout really scared me!

1030
00:36:41,560 --> 00:36:42,240
Don't move.

1031
00:36:42,240 --> 00:36:43,920
(Can't be too careful with this kid)
I'll do it myself, buddy.

1032
00:36:44,400 --> 00:36:45,560
You still don't trust me?

1033
00:36:46,240 --> 00:36:47,760
True. You would've gotten me already.

1034
00:36:47,760 --> 00:36:49,120
If I wanted to get you,

1035
00:36:49,120 --> 00:36:51,240
I could've touched you
like this ages ago!

1036
00:36:51,240 --> 00:36:52,440
(Fellow algae recognize each other)

1037
00:36:52,440 --> 00:36:53,240
Right?

1038
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:54,960
He's a good guy.

1039
00:36:54,960 --> 00:36:56,000
He drew a dolphin.

1040
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:56,840
(Algae (good guys) tasks: 1/7)

1041
00:36:56,840 --> 00:36:58,360
Whose spawn point was this?

1042
00:36:58,360 --> 00:36:59,280
Was it Jingyu's?

1043
00:37:00,040 --> 00:37:01,760
Probably. Anyway, Jingyu and Bing

1044
00:37:01,760 --> 00:37:03,400
seem to be up to something.

1045
00:37:03,700 --> 00:37:06,820
(Keeping a close eye on Mr. Huang)

1046
00:37:06,840 --> 00:37:07,640
Bing went in.

1047
00:37:17,280 --> 00:37:17,840
What?

1048
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:18,640
Are you using the bathroom?

1049
00:37:18,640 --> 00:37:19,400
I just finished.

1050
00:37:26,280 --> 00:37:27,240
You're eliminated.

1051
00:37:27,240 --> 00:37:28,860
(Attack move this round: cheek heart)

1052
00:37:28,880 --> 00:37:30,500
Leaf sheep, open your eyes.

1053
00:37:30,500 --> 00:37:31,260
(Leaf sheep)

1054
00:37:31,300 --> 00:37:33,580
(Jia Bing (algae) gets caught)

1055
00:37:33,660 --> 00:37:36,020
(Eyewitness)

1056
00:37:36,020 --> 00:37:37,740
(Leaf sheep: Huang Jingyu)

1057
00:37:37,740 --> 00:37:39,500
(Caught in the act)

1058
00:37:40,020 --> 00:37:42,020
(I'm screwed)

1059
00:37:44,440 --> 00:37:46,160
Sound the alarm! Hurry!

1060
00:37:46,400 --> 00:37:47,720
(So excited)
Hurry, Bai!

1061
00:37:47,720 --> 00:37:49,880
Bai, hurry!

1062
00:37:51,040 --> 00:37:51,680
Hurry, Bai!

1063
00:37:54,240 --> 00:37:55,160
Hurry!

1064
00:37:56,340 --> 00:37:58,380
(So exciting! One more look)

1065
00:37:58,400 --> 00:37:59,300
Hurry!

1066
00:37:59,940 --> 00:38:02,180
(Speed: 0.000000001/h,
urgency: 9999999.99%)

1067
00:38:02,220 --> 00:38:05,620
(Oh no! They saw everything!)

1068
00:38:06,120 --> 00:38:07,240
No, I think he just...

1069
00:38:07,240 --> 00:38:08,640
He just went to the bathroom.

1070
00:38:10,560 --> 00:38:11,760
Did Bing go to the bathroom?

1071
00:38:12,380 --> 00:38:13,900
Did Bing go to the bathroom?

1072
00:38:14,480 --> 00:38:15,000
What?

1073
00:38:15,520 --> 00:38:16,560
Did Bing go to the bathroom,

1074
00:38:16,560 --> 00:38:17,400
or did you kill him?

1075
00:38:17,840 --> 00:38:18,480
Bathroom.

1076
00:38:18,780 --> 00:38:19,740
(Keep a straight face)

1077
00:38:20,860 --> 00:38:21,740
(Something feels off)

1078
00:38:21,760 --> 00:38:22,320
If...

1079
00:38:23,600 --> 00:38:24,520
Come take a look.

1080
00:38:24,520 --> 00:38:26,080
I thought you took him inside.

1081
00:38:26,080 --> 00:38:26,860
He went to the bathroom.

1082
00:38:27,180 --> 00:38:28,940
(Luring everyone back to the bathroom)

1083
00:38:33,800 --> 00:38:34,520
The three of us...

1084
00:38:34,520 --> 00:38:35,480
Let's watch from here.

1085
00:38:35,480 --> 00:38:37,040
(They bought it)
See if Bing ruins the drawing when he's out.

1086
00:38:38,020 --> 00:38:39,580
(Don't smile!)

1087
00:38:39,620 --> 00:38:41,580
(Back within striking distance)

1088
00:38:41,600 --> 00:38:42,880
Mr. Huang, see if Bing
touches the drawing

1089
00:38:42,880 --> 00:38:43,840
when he comes out.

1090
00:38:44,060 --> 00:38:46,460
(Let me see what Bing's doing)

1091
00:38:48,920 --> 00:38:50,120
Should we hide a little better?

1092
00:38:53,260 --> 00:38:55,180
(Sitting ducks)

1093
00:38:55,200 --> 00:38:56,980
Nine, ten, eleven, twelve.

1094
00:38:56,980 --> 00:38:58,020
(Can attack again
after a 20-second cooldown)

1095
00:38:58,040 --> 00:39:00,160
Thirteen, fourteen, fifteen.

1096
00:39:00,560 --> 00:39:01,920
I think everything's fine,

1097
00:39:02,880 --> 00:39:03,660
right?

1098
00:39:03,660 --> 00:39:05,700
(Bro, haven't I been gone
a little too long?)

1099
00:39:05,740 --> 00:39:07,940
(What's Mr. Huang doing?)

1100
00:39:07,960 --> 00:39:10,000
Eighteen, nineteen, twenty.

1101
00:39:11,340 --> 00:39:12,940
(Cooldown over. Ready to hunt again)

1102
00:39:14,800 --> 00:39:17,080
I can't see very well from here.

1103
00:39:18,180 --> 00:39:20,300
(Time to strike)

1104
00:39:22,220 --> 00:39:24,780
(Can't see. Trying another angle)

1105
00:39:29,640 --> 00:39:30,360
What's taking him so long?

1106
00:39:31,440 --> 00:39:31,960
Number two.

1107
00:39:34,060 --> 00:39:36,220
(Going to check the bathroom)

1108
00:39:36,300 --> 00:39:39,340
(Jingyu's watching closely)

1109
00:39:42,440 --> 00:39:43,080
Bing!

1110
00:39:45,360 --> 00:39:46,440
You're eliminated.

1111
00:39:46,840 --> 00:39:47,360
Bing!

1112
00:39:47,960 --> 00:39:50,500
You're eliminated.

1113
00:39:50,500 --> 00:39:52,940
(Bai Jingting (algae) gets caught)

1114
00:39:56,560 --> 00:39:57,600
Bing!

1115
00:39:58,600 --> 00:39:59,300
Bing!

1116
00:39:59,300 --> 00:40:01,180
(Completely clueless)

1117
00:40:06,500 --> 00:40:09,140
(The hunt is back on)

1118
00:40:14,600 --> 00:40:17,560
Don't move!

1119
00:40:19,260 --> 00:40:21,140
(Stalling through the cooldown)
Don't move!

1120
00:40:21,160 --> 00:40:23,300
(Cooldown over. Ready to hunt again)
Bai, hurry! Sound the alarm!

1121
00:40:24,240 --> 00:40:25,720
Bai, run!

1122
00:40:25,740 --> 00:40:27,340
(Bai's already gone)

1123
00:40:27,340 --> 00:40:29,180
Bai, sound the alarm!

1124
00:40:30,840 --> 00:40:31,440
Someone got killed!

1125
00:40:31,440 --> 00:40:32,320
Someone got killed! Go look!

1126
00:40:32,320 --> 00:40:32,600
Who?

1127
00:40:32,600 --> 00:40:33,200
Go check over there!

1128
00:40:33,200 --> 00:40:33,640
Who?

1129
00:40:33,640 --> 00:40:34,200
Go inside and look!

1130
00:40:34,200 --> 00:40:34,920
Who got killed?

1131
00:40:39,420 --> 00:40:40,820
(Hang in there, buddy)

1132
00:40:43,020 --> 00:40:44,340
(Witnessing it now)

1133
00:40:44,420 --> 00:40:46,300
(A quick glance)

1134
00:40:47,820 --> 00:40:49,540
(Another would-be witness)

1135
00:40:53,840 --> 00:40:55,460
You're eliminated!

1136
00:40:55,460 --> 00:40:56,900
(Wang Anyu (algae) gets caught)

1137
00:40:56,940 --> 00:40:59,140
(Not even water can save him)

1138
00:41:01,820 --> 00:41:04,340
(The only eyewitness (mascot edition))

1139
00:41:08,920 --> 00:41:10,200
Bai got killed!

1140
00:41:10,200 --> 00:41:11,480
Bai, did you get killed?

1141
00:41:13,440 --> 00:41:14,400
Bai's dead!

1142
00:41:14,400 --> 00:41:14,840
Who?

1143
00:41:14,840 --> 00:41:15,200
I didn't see anything!

1144
00:41:15,200 --> 00:41:16,440
Sound the alarm!

1145
00:41:18,160 --> 00:41:18,720
Sound the alarm!

1146
00:41:23,320 --> 00:41:25,480
It's Huang Jingyu!

1147
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:26,480
Sound the alarm!

1148
00:41:28,060 --> 00:41:30,780
(Just arrived at the crime scene)

1149
00:41:30,820 --> 00:41:32,060
(Plenty of witnesses,
but they only saw the aftermath)

1150
00:41:32,080 --> 00:41:32,480
Sound the alarm!

1151
00:41:33,160 --> 00:41:34,600
He can't kill anyone now! Hurry!

1152
00:41:34,600 --> 00:41:35,520
I'll raise my hand.

1153
00:41:37,760 --> 00:41:39,200
Come back, everyone.

1154
00:41:39,920 --> 00:41:40,720
If we go together,

1155
00:41:40,720 --> 00:41:41,960
(Acting like a prophet)
we might both get eliminated.

1156
00:41:41,960 --> 00:41:42,880
We look like idiots!

1157
00:41:42,880 --> 00:41:43,440
Can't we say survive?

1158
00:41:43,440 --> 00:41:44,560
We look like complete idiots!

1159
00:41:46,140 --> 00:41:48,100
(Underwater villagers sound the alarm)

1160
00:41:48,120 --> 00:41:48,880
Who sounded the alarm?

1161
00:41:49,520 --> 00:41:50,360
Teng.

1162
00:41:50,360 --> 00:41:51,760
Two got killed?

1163
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:53,040
Three!

1164
00:41:53,620 --> 00:41:56,060
(Quite the killing spree)
At least three.

1165
00:41:58,050 --> 00:41:59,040
(Underwater meeting, round 2)
It has to be Jingyu.

1166
00:41:59,040 --> 00:42:00,320
There's no one else.

1167
00:42:00,320 --> 00:42:01,960
Why does it have to be me?

1168
00:42:01,960 --> 00:42:02,600
Who else could it be?

1169
00:42:03,480 --> 00:42:04,560
There were three of us together.

1170
00:42:04,560 --> 00:42:05,760
Everyone else got killed.

1171
00:42:05,960 --> 00:42:07,640
I'm the only eyewitness now.

1172
00:42:08,740 --> 00:42:10,140
(Holding back)

1173
00:42:10,160 --> 00:42:11,200
Everyone over there is dead!

1174
00:42:11,200 --> 00:42:11,880
You're the only one left!

1175
00:42:11,880 --> 00:42:13,200
You're an eyewitness?

1176
00:42:13,200 --> 00:42:14,880
Then who did you see kill whom?

1177
00:42:14,880 --> 00:42:15,840
The three of us,

1178
00:42:15,840 --> 00:42:17,200
Bai, Anyu, and me,

1179
00:42:17,200 --> 00:42:18,880
went into that room together.

1180
00:42:18,880 --> 00:42:20,480
Then I needed the bathroom.

1181
00:42:20,480 --> 00:42:21,680
So I went in.

1182
00:42:21,680 --> 00:42:22,720
They both left.

1183
00:42:22,720 --> 00:42:23,880
When I came out,

1184
00:42:23,880 --> 00:42:24,800
Bing was by the door.

1185
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:25,720
There was a drawing there.

1186
00:42:26,560 --> 00:42:27,400
But he didn't ruin it.

1187
00:42:27,400 --> 00:42:28,560
Bing said he needed the bathroom.

1188
00:42:29,320 --> 00:42:30,640
(Just watching you make excuses)
I said, "Sure, go ahead."

1189
00:42:30,640 --> 00:42:31,440
Then I went outside.

1190
00:42:31,440 --> 00:42:33,120
Those two were by the window.

1191
00:42:33,120 --> 00:42:34,120
One stood, one crouched.

1192
00:42:34,120 --> 00:42:35,280
They were peeking inside.

1193
00:42:35,280 --> 00:42:37,440
Then we were by the bathroom door.

1194
00:42:37,440 --> 00:42:38,680
I said I'd stay and watch

1195
00:42:38,680 --> 00:42:39,320
for Bing to come out

1196
00:42:39,320 --> 00:42:39,920
and see if he ruined the drawing.

1197
00:42:39,920 --> 00:42:40,440
I waited a bit.

1198
00:42:40,440 --> 00:42:41,200
Bing didn't come out.

1199
00:42:41,200 --> 00:42:42,480
So I left.

1200
00:42:42,480 --> 00:42:43,360
As I was leaving,

1201
00:42:43,360 --> 00:42:44,640
Wang Anyu came in.

1202
00:42:44,640 --> 00:42:46,040
Then I went to talk to Bai.

1203
00:42:46,040 --> 00:42:47,920
He was already dead.

1204
00:42:47,920 --> 00:42:49,280
I figured Anyu had to be the killer.

1205
00:42:49,280 --> 00:42:50,840
But when I went back to catch him,

1206
00:42:50,840 --> 00:42:51,680
Bing was already dead.

1207
00:42:52,640 --> 00:42:54,080
And now Anyu's dead too.

1208
00:42:54,080 --> 00:42:56,240
Then he tried to make a move on me,

1209
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:57,580
so I slapped his water away.

1210
00:42:58,020 --> 00:42:59,380
(The silent scapegoat)

1211
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:04,280
Wait, if Anyu ran out of water

1212
00:43:04,280 --> 00:43:05,680
and he was the wolf,

1213
00:43:05,680 --> 00:43:07,160
wouldn't the game be over?

1214
00:43:08,360 --> 00:43:10,120
Would the game really end
if the wolf ran out?

1215
00:43:10,120 --> 00:43:11,120
Then we'd all be good guys.

1216
00:43:11,120 --> 00:43:12,120
Who would we be voting for?

1217
00:43:12,120 --> 00:43:12,800
Exactly!

1218
00:43:12,800 --> 00:43:14,040
If the wolf ran out of water,

1219
00:43:14,480 --> 00:43:16,160
(Yep, exactly what you're thinking)
wouldn't the game be over?

1220
00:43:16,160 --> 00:43:17,920
(Desperately holding on)
They'd just end it? No way!

1221
00:43:18,120 --> 00:43:19,760
Then why are we voting?

1222
00:43:19,760 --> 00:43:22,240
If we're all good guys,
who are we voting for?

1223
00:43:22,720 --> 00:43:24,040
It's Huang Jingyu!

1224
00:43:24,720 --> 00:43:25,320
Teng,

1225
00:43:26,240 --> 00:43:27,640
open your eyes!

1226
00:43:27,640 --> 00:43:28,680
It's you, ten thousand percent.

1227
00:43:30,160 --> 00:43:31,040
His water got knocked out.

1228
00:43:31,040 --> 00:43:32,000
The wolf is dead.

1229
00:43:32,000 --> 00:43:33,380
So we're all good guys now.

1230
00:43:33,460 --> 00:43:35,420
What a genius!

1231
00:43:36,140 --> 00:43:37,260
(There's no talking his way out of this)

1232
00:43:37,280 --> 00:43:38,720
Look, his eyes are turning red.

1233
00:43:39,240 --> 00:43:41,520
Here comes
that almost-crying face again.

1234
00:43:41,520 --> 00:43:43,120
I went on a killing spree!

1235
00:43:45,040 --> 00:43:46,760
He's not upset about losing.

1236
00:43:46,760 --> 00:43:47,280
He's upset

1237
00:43:47,280 --> 00:43:48,660
he'll never play a cop again.

1238
00:43:48,660 --> 00:43:50,620
(It's okay. You're a great actor)

1239
00:43:53,560 --> 00:43:54,160
Let's do it.

1240
00:43:55,700 --> 00:43:56,500
(Huang Jingyu x3, Shen Teng x1)

1241
00:43:56,520 --> 00:43:57,960
Game

1242
00:43:57,960 --> 00:43:58,480
over.

1243
00:43:58,920 --> 00:44:00,560
There was no talking my way out of that!

1244
00:44:01,640 --> 00:44:02,520
Four people in one room.

1245
00:44:02,520 --> 00:44:03,680
I killed three of them!

1246
00:44:04,040 --> 00:44:06,680
You actually managed to kill us both!

1247
00:44:06,680 --> 00:44:07,400
I'm telling you, you really...

1248
00:44:07,400 --> 00:44:07,920
You just...

1249
00:44:07,920 --> 00:44:08,280
You really...

1250
00:44:08,280 --> 00:44:10,240
Your timing was perfect!

1251
00:44:10,880 --> 00:44:12,480
You killed so fast!

1252
00:44:12,480 --> 00:44:15,520
After he took out Bing,

1253
00:44:15,520 --> 00:44:16,120
he came out and told us

1254
00:44:16,120 --> 00:44:17,400
Bing was taking a dump!

1255
00:44:19,840 --> 00:44:20,880
And we were like,

1256
00:44:20,880 --> 00:44:21,760
okay.

1257
00:44:23,560 --> 00:44:24,760
- We were standing there like idiots!
- He told us to wait outside.

1258
00:44:24,760 --> 00:44:25,360
So we stayed outside!

1259
00:44:25,360 --> 00:44:25,600
I...

1260
00:44:27,600 --> 00:44:28,760
You two were pretty clueless!

1261
00:44:28,760 --> 00:44:30,640
The glass looks dark from outside.

1262
00:44:30,640 --> 00:44:32,120
But you can see everything from inside!

1263
00:44:32,120 --> 00:44:32,800
You know?

1264
00:44:34,760 --> 00:44:35,760
The worst part was

1265
00:44:35,760 --> 00:44:36,960
when he knocked and called, "Bing!"

1266
00:44:37,520 --> 00:44:38,200
"Bing!"

1267
00:44:38,200 --> 00:44:39,320
And I couldn't say a word!

1268
00:44:41,480 --> 00:44:43,200
You two found a loophole.

1269
00:44:43,200 --> 00:44:44,040
You couldn't come out,

1270
00:44:44,040 --> 00:44:44,760
and he was too embarrassed to go in!

1271
00:44:44,760 --> 00:44:45,200
Exactly!

1272
00:44:46,080 --> 00:44:47,460
He really thought I was pooping!

1273
00:44:47,500 --> 00:44:49,420
(Ignorance is bliss)

1274
00:44:49,520 --> 00:44:50,400
Alright, everyone.

1275
00:44:50,400 --> 00:44:51,880
Let's rinse off in the pool.

1276
00:44:51,880 --> 00:44:52,120
Come on!

1277
00:44:52,120 --> 00:44:52,440
Okay!

1278
00:44:54,880 --> 00:44:56,240
I'm the most soaked.

1279
00:44:57,680 --> 00:44:58,400
Change into swimsuits.

1280
00:45:30,240 --> 00:45:31,920
Into the pool!

1281
00:45:33,320 --> 00:45:38,800
Chinese people can fly!

1282
00:45:38,800 --> 00:45:40,220
You didn't even miss that joke!

1283
00:45:40,220 --> 00:45:40,900
(What if you miss a joke?)

1284
00:45:41,840 --> 00:45:42,880
Our next challenge

1285
00:45:42,880 --> 00:45:44,640
is called Rhythm Master.

1286
00:45:44,640 --> 00:45:48,200
(Rhythm Master rules)
The challenger points up, down, left,

1287
00:45:48,200 --> 00:45:49,440
(Round-robin matches)
or right.

1288
00:45:49,440 --> 00:45:50,680
(Last person on land wins)
The opponent

1289
00:45:50,680 --> 00:45:52,680
must quickly turn their head

1290
00:45:52,680 --> 00:45:53,440
in one direction.

1291
00:45:53,440 --> 00:45:54,600
If the directions match,

1292
00:45:54,600 --> 00:45:55,680
the opponent loses

1293
00:45:55,680 --> 00:45:57,040
and gets pushed into the pool.

1294
00:45:57,600 --> 00:45:59,680
So we're finally letting out

1295
00:45:59,680 --> 00:46:01,680
(Time for revenge)
all that frustration from the last game?

1296
00:46:03,320 --> 00:46:05,360
In this round, we've got

1297
00:46:05,360 --> 00:46:06,680
Taobao's bigger surprises!

1298
00:46:06,680 --> 00:46:07,680
Complete the special challenge

1299
00:46:07,680 --> 00:46:08,880
and the winner unlocks

1300
00:46:08,880 --> 00:46:10,160
the magic magnifying glass

1301
00:46:10,160 --> 00:46:12,520
and a Taobao outdoor gear gift box!

1302
00:46:12,520 --> 00:46:13,800
These will make

1303
00:46:13,800 --> 00:46:16,040
our upcoming adventures
even more exciting!

1304
00:46:19,600 --> 00:46:20,480
Catch that "ooh".

1305
00:46:25,540 --> 00:46:26,420
(Failed)

1306
00:46:28,080 --> 00:46:29,160
I couldn't react in time.

1307
00:46:29,440 --> 00:46:31,240
Anyu, Hu, give us a demo.

1308
00:46:31,240 --> 00:46:31,800
Okay.

1309
00:46:31,860 --> 00:46:33,900
(Special challenge)

1310
00:46:48,440 --> 00:46:49,040
Check it out.

1311
00:46:49,040 --> 00:46:50,120
This list is packed

1312
00:46:50,120 --> 00:46:51,680
with great outdoor essentials.

1313
00:46:51,680 --> 00:46:53,400
Taobao really has everything!

1314
00:46:53,400 --> 00:46:54,640
Now I'll use Taobao's magnifying glass

1315
00:46:54,640 --> 00:46:55,600
to make them bigger!

1316
00:46:56,960 --> 00:46:59,120
We're also giving away

1317
00:46:59,120 --> 00:47:00,800
these awesome outdoor essentials!

1318
00:47:00,800 --> 00:47:02,520
Search "Natural High" on Taobao

1319
00:47:02,520 --> 00:47:04,440
for a chance to win

1320
00:47:04,440 --> 00:47:05,880
the same outdoor gear on our list!

1321
00:47:05,880 --> 00:47:06,600
Share it with friends

1322
00:47:06,600 --> 00:47:09,080
to unlock even more rewards and fun!

1323
00:47:09,080 --> 00:47:11,360
You could also win
a handwritten postcard from Wanning

1324
00:47:11,360 --> 00:47:14,120
or an 888-yuan travel fund!

1325
00:47:14,120 --> 00:47:15,720
New prizes every day!

1326
00:47:16,000 --> 00:47:16,680
Plus,

1327
00:47:16,680 --> 00:47:18,120
search "Natural High" on Taobao

1328
00:47:18,120 --> 00:47:19,640
and reserve a spot for our livestream!

1329
00:47:19,640 --> 00:47:21,400
Tons of surprises and rewards await!

1330
00:47:25,820 --> 00:47:26,420
(Rhythm Master officially begins)

1331
00:47:26,440 --> 00:47:27,140
Start!

1332
00:47:28,180 --> 00:47:31,300
(Getting into the rhythm)

1333
00:47:35,840 --> 00:47:36,360
Watch out!

1334
00:47:38,220 --> 00:47:38,820
(Off you go)

1335
00:47:50,040 --> 00:47:50,860
Bing's good!

1336
00:47:52,500 --> 00:47:54,060
(Spoke too soon)

1337
00:47:56,780 --> 00:47:57,980
(Panicking)

1338
00:48:01,680 --> 00:48:02,720
Hu's good.

1339
00:48:02,720 --> 00:48:03,660
(Already beaten three people)
Hu's good.

1340
00:48:10,420 --> 00:48:11,820
(Another case of speaking too soon)

1341
00:48:11,960 --> 00:48:12,280
Go!

1342
00:48:23,900 --> 00:48:24,620
(I'm outta here)

1343
00:48:25,260 --> 00:48:27,460
(Half-turn in midair)

1344
00:48:29,120 --> 00:48:30,600
You can even turn in midair?

1345
00:48:30,600 --> 00:48:32,200
(Bai Jingting can fly)
Chinese people can fly!

1346
00:48:38,980 --> 00:48:39,940
(Almost showed his true colors)

1347
00:48:53,460 --> 00:48:54,380
(Fakes left, strikes right)

1348
00:48:56,220 --> 00:48:57,220
(That's sneaky)

1349
00:48:57,960 --> 00:48:59,040
He goes like this!

1350
00:48:59,040 --> 00:49:00,960
And then this! Like that!

1351
00:49:00,960 --> 00:49:04,060
That's cheating!

1352
00:49:04,060 --> 00:49:05,020
(Using both hands)

1353
00:49:09,160 --> 00:49:09,920
Bring it on!

1354
00:49:12,280 --> 00:49:13,400
Mr. Huang wins.

1355
00:49:13,400 --> 00:49:14,100
Mr. Huang!

1356
00:49:14,100 --> 00:49:15,180
(The Rhythm Master, Huang Jingyu)

1357
00:49:15,200 --> 00:49:16,480
Impressive.

1358
00:49:16,480 --> 00:49:17,920
I owe it all to my teammates.

1359
00:49:18,640 --> 00:49:18,880
Wait,

1360
00:49:18,880 --> 00:49:20,440
so you only played
against one person, then?

1361
00:49:21,060 --> 00:49:22,300
(This master is less impressive
than he seems)

1362
00:49:22,360 --> 00:49:23,560
Impressive.

1363
00:49:23,560 --> 00:49:24,120
Will Dr. Chen

1364
00:49:24,120 --> 00:49:25,920
resurface any moment now?

1365
00:49:27,880 --> 00:49:28,840
Come on.

1366
00:49:28,840 --> 00:49:29,840
Let's play together.

1367
00:49:29,840 --> 00:49:30,760
Get in.

1368
00:49:32,480 --> 00:49:33,600
There is even someone diving.

1369
00:49:34,980 --> 00:49:36,140
(What a jellyfish hairstyle)

1370
00:49:36,160 --> 00:49:37,520
We have come to Hainan this time.

1371
00:49:37,520 --> 00:49:38,720
There is a fish here that helps

1372
00:49:38,720 --> 00:49:41,160
(Materials sourced from the internet)
larger fish remove parasites

1373
00:49:41,160 --> 00:49:42,640
and recover their health.

1374
00:49:42,640 --> 00:49:44,440
It is known as the doctor of the sea,

1375
00:49:44,440 --> 00:49:45,760
(Bluestreak cleaner wrasse)
the bluestreak cleaner wrasse.

1376
00:49:45,760 --> 00:49:47,680
However, there is another fish
that looks very similar.

1377
00:49:47,680 --> 00:49:49,520
(Bluestriped fangblenny)
It is called the bluestriped fangblenny.

1378
00:49:49,520 --> 00:49:51,340
It mimics
the cleaner wrasse's appearance

1379
00:49:51,340 --> 00:49:52,560
(Bluestreak cleaner wrasse)
and swimming patterns

1380
00:49:52,560 --> 00:49:53,880
(vs. bluestriped fangblenny)
to blend in with them.

1381
00:49:53,880 --> 00:49:56,800
When larger fish let their guard down,

1382
00:49:56,800 --> 00:49:58,680
it suddenly bites them to get food.

1383
00:50:00,120 --> 00:50:01,360
The next challenge is called

1384
00:50:01,360 --> 00:50:02,760
"Mischievous Fish Doctor".

1385
00:50:02,760 --> 00:50:04,120
There are six cleaner fish here

1386
00:50:04,120 --> 00:50:05,800
(Mischievous Fish Doctor: Rules)
and two mischievous fish.

1387
00:50:05,800 --> 00:50:07,680
(Five fish per platform for 10 seconds)
Cleaner fish must unlock

1388
00:50:07,680 --> 00:50:09,600
(Cleaner fish must unlock all platforms)
all three shrinking platforms.

1389
00:50:09,600 --> 00:50:11,600
(Identifying both impostors
also wins the mission)

1390
00:50:11,800 --> 00:50:13,180
(Impostors must stay hidden
and sabotage the mission)

1391
00:50:13,180 --> 00:50:13,800
At least five fish

1392
00:50:13,800 --> 00:50:15,360
must stay on each platform
for 10 seconds

1393
00:50:15,360 --> 00:50:17,440
to unlock the next one.

1394
00:50:17,440 --> 00:50:19,440
The two mischievous fish must conceal

1395
00:50:19,440 --> 00:50:20,600
their identities and disrupt

1396
00:50:20,800 --> 00:50:21,480
the others to prevent

1397
00:50:21,480 --> 00:50:23,120
the cleaner fish
from completing the challenge.

1398
00:50:23,120 --> 00:50:24,140
Where are you pushing me?

1399
00:50:25,120 --> 00:50:25,680
Come on.

1400
00:50:25,680 --> 00:50:27,480
Let us hand out the identity cards.

1401
00:50:27,480 --> 00:50:28,120
Come on.

1402
00:50:36,040 --> 00:50:36,440
Come on.

1403
00:50:36,440 --> 00:50:36,840
Come.

1404
00:50:37,440 --> 00:50:38,800
Can we play while staying in the water?

1405
00:50:38,820 --> 00:50:39,520
(Too lazy to get out)

1406
00:50:39,520 --> 00:50:40,400
Not getting out?

1407
00:50:40,840 --> 00:50:42,300
How are you so good at doing nothing?

1408
00:50:42,940 --> 00:50:43,900
(Notice: Subtitles lowered
for better visibility)

1409
00:50:43,920 --> 00:50:44,940
(Showing off his handsome face)
Hurry up.

1410
00:50:44,980 --> 00:50:47,260
(Mr. Hu catches fish)

1411
00:50:47,260 --> 00:50:48,380
(Teng refuses to cooperate)

1412
00:50:48,560 --> 00:50:49,700
One, two, go.

1413
00:50:49,700 --> 00:50:51,620
(Atlantic salmon)

1414
00:50:51,860 --> 00:50:52,740
(Deadlift: 77 kg.
Season 2 record updated)

1415
00:50:52,760 --> 00:50:53,840
Do not pull the ring off.

1416
00:50:54,660 --> 00:50:57,140
(A trained athlete comes
to help: Atlantic salmon)

1417
00:50:58,300 --> 00:50:59,980
(Successfully hauled ashore)

1418
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:01,200
Come on, Teng.

1419
00:51:01,220 --> 00:51:02,260
(You are not moving at all, right?)

1420
00:51:02,280 --> 00:51:03,480
You are not putting in any effort.

1421
00:51:06,880 --> 00:51:08,280
The two mischievous fish may identify

1422
00:51:08,280 --> 00:51:09,260
each other this round.

1423
00:51:09,260 --> 00:51:10,540
(Impostors may identify each other)
Please close your eyes.

1424
00:51:14,480 --> 00:51:15,400
Mischievous Fish,

1425
00:51:15,400 --> 00:51:16,880
open your eyes and identify each other.

1426
00:51:18,300 --> 00:51:20,900
(Mischievous Fish:
Fan Chengcheng and Wang Anyu)

1427
00:51:26,680 --> 00:51:27,720
Begin.

1428
00:51:27,720 --> 00:51:28,140
Come on.

1429
00:51:28,140 --> 00:51:28,700
(Mischievous Fish:
Fan Chengcheng and Wang Anyu)

1430
00:51:28,700 --> 00:51:29,420
(Mischievous Fish Doctor,
First game, Round 1)

1431
00:51:29,440 --> 00:51:30,400
Can we please

1432
00:51:30,400 --> 00:51:32,240
not cause trouble in the first round?

1433
00:51:32,240 --> 00:51:34,560
(Loud enough for his teammates to hear)
Let's get on together first.

1434
00:51:34,560 --> 00:51:35,480
(Understood)
Let's all get up there first.

1435
00:51:35,480 --> 00:51:36,160
Go ahead.

1436
00:51:36,160 --> 00:51:36,960
I am going.

1437
00:51:39,060 --> 00:51:42,220
(Steady progress, one step at a time)

1438
00:51:50,560 --> 00:51:52,200
You look rather intimidating.

1439
00:51:57,360 --> 00:51:58,600
Let's see who can knock me down.

1440
00:51:59,980 --> 00:52:01,140
(My muscles are not made of dough)

1441
00:52:02,780 --> 00:52:04,100
(Let us see who dares to cause trouble)

1442
00:52:04,500 --> 00:52:05,520
I am coming, Bing.

1443
00:52:05,520 --> 00:52:06,420
Come on, you can do it.

1444
00:52:06,460 --> 00:52:08,540
(Mischievous fish makes its move)

1445
00:52:09,180 --> 00:52:10,900
(Watching closely)

1446
00:52:11,060 --> 00:52:11,780
Good.

1447
00:52:11,780 --> 00:52:13,100
(Catches him in one swift move)

1448
00:52:14,180 --> 00:52:15,020
(Trapped)

1449
00:52:16,000 --> 00:52:17,480
(Waiting for a chance to strike)
I can move further in.

1450
00:52:17,480 --> 00:52:17,960
Go further in.

1451
00:52:17,960 --> 00:52:19,000
(Squeezing through)
Do not bend your knees.

1452
00:52:19,000 --> 00:52:21,180
(Squeezing through)
I can reach a little farther in.

1453
00:52:21,340 --> 00:52:22,460
(Come on, teammate)

1454
00:52:22,500 --> 00:52:24,020
(Doing his best)

1455
00:52:24,080 --> 00:52:25,820
Come on, sit on my face!

1456
00:52:25,820 --> 00:52:27,700
(Going all out, losing all restraint)

1457
00:52:28,600 --> 00:52:29,440
Bai,

1458
00:52:29,680 --> 00:52:30,800
I am barely holding on.

1459
00:52:30,800 --> 00:52:32,840
Can't you get onto that foam
platform over there?

1460
00:52:32,840 --> 00:52:33,400
I already am.

1461
00:52:35,120 --> 00:52:36,360
Jingyu.

1462
00:52:36,360 --> 00:52:38,080
It definitely cannot be Jingyu.

1463
00:52:38,080 --> 00:52:38,920
He is trying way too hard.

1464
00:52:40,020 --> 00:52:41,220
(Stay low for now)
Teng, go ahead.

1465
00:52:41,240 --> 00:52:42,320
Is that Bo Erteng?

1466
00:52:44,340 --> 00:52:46,700
(Time to show off his true skills)

1467
00:52:49,580 --> 00:52:50,780
(That is all he has to show)

1468
00:52:52,520 --> 00:52:54,080
Look how hard Teng is trying this round.

1469
00:52:54,080 --> 00:52:54,840
He went up early.

1470
00:52:54,840 --> 00:52:55,920
That is suspicious.

1471
00:52:57,400 --> 00:52:58,760
I refuse to speak to any of you.

1472
00:52:58,900 --> 00:53:00,900
(Doing his best)

1473
00:53:02,160 --> 00:53:03,120
Wait...

1474
00:53:03,480 --> 00:53:04,520
Can we fit more people up here?

1475
00:53:04,780 --> 00:53:05,420
(Trapped with no room to move)

1476
00:53:05,440 --> 00:53:06,560
Careful. Here I come.

1477
00:53:09,640 --> 00:53:11,640
Teng, your foot.

1478
00:53:12,280 --> 00:53:14,360
If I put my foot down,

1479
00:53:14,360 --> 00:53:16,280
I will have to rely on my core strength.

1480
00:53:16,720 --> 00:53:19,320
That is precisely what Teng lacks.

1481
00:53:19,420 --> 00:53:20,580
(You sly Hu Sanyao)

1482
00:53:22,240 --> 00:53:23,240
I will go first.

1483
00:53:23,240 --> 00:53:24,120
Come on.

1484
00:53:24,300 --> 00:53:25,820
(Mischievous Fish No. 2 makes its move)

1485
00:53:29,320 --> 00:53:29,880
You can sit on top.

1486
00:53:34,340 --> 00:53:35,940
(Eagerly volunteers to help)

1487
00:53:35,980 --> 00:53:37,460
(One man on top of another)

1488
00:53:38,900 --> 00:53:40,660
(A commuter using a phone
while carrying a child)

1489
00:53:40,660 --> 00:53:41,540
(I cannot hold on much longer)

1490
00:53:41,820 --> 00:53:43,340
(Bing, your rescue team is on the way)

1491
00:53:48,380 --> 00:53:50,700
(A professional entry into the water)

1492
00:53:51,620 --> 00:53:52,620
(An unexpected surprise)

1493
00:53:54,840 --> 00:53:55,440
Bing.

1494
00:53:55,880 --> 00:53:57,360
(Immediately joins the group)
It has to be Bing.

1495
00:53:57,360 --> 00:53:59,480
Bing, I even managed to get up
there despite the struggle.

1496
00:53:59,700 --> 00:54:01,340
(Desperately trying
to prove his innocence)

1497
00:54:01,360 --> 00:54:02,920
What is wrong with you, Bing?

1498
00:54:05,360 --> 00:54:06,580
What is wrong with you, Bing?

1499
00:54:06,620 --> 00:54:08,460
(Playing now: Dripping)
♪I'm dripping wet in the lake♪

1500
00:54:08,500 --> 00:54:09,580
♪The water's so murky♪

1501
00:54:09,620 --> 00:54:11,740
♪It's already up to my knees♪

1502
00:54:11,760 --> 00:54:13,400
What is wrong with you, Bing?

1503
00:54:13,740 --> 00:54:14,900
(My teammate)

1504
00:54:16,760 --> 00:54:17,160
No.

1505
00:54:17,160 --> 00:54:18,600
(Suspicion arises)
That is not...

1506
00:54:18,600 --> 00:54:19,320
That doesn't count.

1507
00:54:19,320 --> 00:54:19,760
Teng.

1508
00:54:19,760 --> 00:54:20,480
(Give me back my teammate)
That doesn't count.

1509
00:54:20,480 --> 00:54:21,120
Teng.

1510
00:54:21,120 --> 00:54:22,080
That doesn't count.

1511
00:54:22,100 --> 00:54:23,460
(What does it mean?)

1512
00:54:23,480 --> 00:54:24,400
It counts.

1513
00:54:24,500 --> 00:54:26,460
(Fine, then)

1514
00:54:26,480 --> 00:54:27,380
That move of yours...

1515
00:54:27,380 --> 00:54:28,260
(You owe us an explanation)

1516
00:54:28,280 --> 00:54:29,480
Then I'll get in the water for you.

1517
00:54:29,480 --> 00:54:29,920
Do not.

1518
00:54:29,920 --> 00:54:30,800
(Not a threat)
Go ahead and play.

1519
00:54:30,800 --> 00:54:31,560
Once this round is over,

1520
00:54:31,560 --> 00:54:33,120
you will be down here with me.

1521
00:54:33,120 --> 00:54:33,640
All right.

1522
00:54:33,860 --> 00:54:35,260
(Only one impostor remains
on the platform)

1523
00:54:39,700 --> 00:54:41,060
(Wang, it is all up to you now)

1524
00:54:43,820 --> 00:54:44,540
(First platform unlocked)

1525
00:54:44,560 --> 00:54:45,360
Let's go.

1526
00:54:45,820 --> 00:54:47,740
(Missed opportunity)

1527
00:54:47,760 --> 00:54:48,160
Go.

1528
00:54:50,580 --> 00:54:52,300
(A bad idea is taking brewing)

1529
00:55:02,400 --> 00:55:03,040
I am coming.

1530
00:55:03,060 --> 00:55:04,460
(Makes the first move)

1531
00:55:04,500 --> 00:55:05,780
(You are our only hope)

1532
00:55:05,820 --> 00:55:07,540
(Watching from the sidelines)

1533
00:55:07,560 --> 00:55:08,160
Good.

1534
00:55:08,520 --> 00:55:09,480
Teng, come on.

1535
00:55:09,920 --> 00:55:11,280
Teng, you owe us an explanation.

1536
00:55:11,380 --> 00:55:12,970
(The fish under the greatest suspicion)
Would I really stoop

1537
00:55:12,970 --> 00:55:14,160
to such underhanded tactics?

1538
00:55:14,220 --> 00:55:15,460
(At least try something
more sophisticated)

1539
00:55:15,960 --> 00:55:17,400
Come on, engage your core.

1540
00:55:17,400 --> 00:55:18,660
(Defense mode activated)
He is coming.

1541
00:55:19,060 --> 00:55:19,600
Okay.

1542
00:55:20,640 --> 00:55:22,200
I thought you told me to engage my core.

1543
00:55:22,880 --> 00:55:24,000
We are bracing ourselves.

1544
00:55:24,240 --> 00:55:25,280
I am still here...

1545
00:55:26,120 --> 00:55:27,720
Still breathing.

1546
00:55:30,560 --> 00:55:31,080
Do not push.

1547
00:55:31,080 --> 00:55:31,720
Hold him in place.

1548
00:55:32,100 --> 00:55:33,300
(You will not get away
with causing trouble)

1549
00:55:33,320 --> 00:55:34,040
Do not push.

1550
00:55:34,880 --> 00:55:35,960
I can feel the pressure

1551
00:55:35,960 --> 00:55:37,620
from every direction now.

1552
00:55:37,620 --> 00:55:38,420
(Activating the blame-shifting skill)

1553
00:55:38,440 --> 00:55:39,180
Except behind you.

1554
00:55:39,180 --> 00:55:39,900
(Not putting any pressure on you)

1555
00:55:39,920 --> 00:55:41,280
I have not even touched you.

1556
00:55:41,620 --> 00:55:42,700
(Too risky to act. Keeps watching)

1557
00:55:42,720 --> 00:55:44,200
I would not even
dare stand next to Teng.

1558
00:55:44,800 --> 00:55:46,120
Move your hand.

1559
00:55:46,720 --> 00:55:48,120
It is too easy for you to push me.

1560
00:55:48,120 --> 00:55:49,320
Too easy for you to push me.

1561
00:55:49,320 --> 00:55:51,740
(Even you suspect me?)
You think I can easily push you?

1562
00:55:51,780 --> 00:55:53,580
(Someone else can finally
take the blame)

1563
00:55:58,580 --> 00:55:59,860
(It is time to make a move)

1564
00:56:00,300 --> 00:56:02,300
(Make a move or stay put?)

1565
00:56:02,300 --> 00:56:03,220
(Too frightened to move)

1566
00:56:03,600 --> 00:56:04,580
(Second platform unlocked)
Hurry. Move.

1567
00:56:04,620 --> 00:56:05,780
(Cowardly, but feeling perfectly safe)

1568
00:56:05,800 --> 00:56:06,560
Let's go.

1569
00:56:06,560 --> 00:56:06,920
Go.

1570
00:56:08,120 --> 00:56:09,920
We cannot let Teng
make the first move again.

1571
00:56:10,420 --> 00:56:12,300
(You fool, Hu Sanyao)
It could be Bai.

1572
00:56:12,420 --> 00:56:13,580
(Keep suspecting one another)

1573
00:56:13,880 --> 00:56:15,760
Just stay seated, okay?

1574
00:56:16,120 --> 00:56:18,520
You can use your strength
to hold them back.

1575
00:56:19,140 --> 00:56:20,220
(The base is set)

1576
00:56:20,240 --> 00:56:20,800
I am coming.

1577
00:56:20,800 --> 00:56:21,260
Come on.

1578
00:56:21,260 --> 00:56:22,780
(You are all done for)

1579
00:56:29,380 --> 00:56:31,180
(Deliberately leaning forward)

1580
00:56:31,260 --> 00:56:32,500
(Is it going to work?)

1581
00:56:36,220 --> 00:56:37,700
(Hold on tight)

1582
00:56:38,180 --> 00:56:38,900
(The base catches him)

1583
00:56:38,900 --> 00:56:39,700
(How is he managing to hold on?)

1584
00:56:40,120 --> 00:56:40,600
Good.

1585
00:56:40,660 --> 00:56:41,660
(Just a little more)

1586
00:56:42,100 --> 00:56:43,140
(So close, yet so far)

1587
00:56:43,160 --> 00:56:44,800
Everyone, engage your core.

1588
00:56:46,740 --> 00:56:48,540
(I need another plan)

1589
00:56:48,560 --> 00:56:49,680
Which side should I charge at?

1590
00:56:49,680 --> 00:56:50,380
Sit down.

1591
00:56:50,380 --> 00:56:50,940
(Helping him sit down)

1592
00:56:51,400 --> 00:56:52,700
Do not tickle me.

1593
00:56:52,700 --> 00:56:53,180
(Holding him down)

1594
00:56:53,660 --> 00:56:55,980
(One on each side.
Everything is under control)

1595
00:56:56,440 --> 00:56:57,000
You four...

1596
00:56:59,440 --> 00:57:01,120
Could someone help with my heels?

1597
00:57:02,040 --> 00:57:03,960
(Under immense pressure)
Look how much weight they are carrying.

1598
00:57:03,960 --> 00:57:05,600
Shift your center of gravity
forward a little.

1599
00:57:06,500 --> 00:57:07,380
(The impostor is relying heavily
on his teammates)

1600
00:57:07,900 --> 00:57:08,780
(Arm lock and shoulder carry)

1601
00:57:08,800 --> 00:57:10,280
Do not tip me over like that.

1602
00:57:10,380 --> 00:57:11,340
(Mischievous Fish grabs him
in one swift move)

1603
00:57:11,360 --> 00:57:12,240
Teng is coming.

1604
00:57:12,540 --> 00:57:13,500
(The opportunity has arrived)

1605
00:57:13,520 --> 00:57:14,540
There is no room left to stand.

1606
00:57:14,580 --> 00:57:15,900
(Fish Doctor needs one more fish
to complete the challenge)

1607
00:57:15,920 --> 00:57:16,520
I will do it.

1608
00:57:19,040 --> 00:57:19,640
Teng is here.

1609
00:57:19,640 --> 00:57:20,380
Hold Teng in place.

1610
00:57:20,380 --> 00:57:21,180
(You are now trapped by me)

1611
00:57:21,200 --> 00:57:22,200
Keep him under control.

1612
00:57:22,200 --> 00:57:23,240
Teng is coming.

1613
00:57:23,240 --> 00:57:26,720
At this rate, we are done for.

1614
00:57:28,080 --> 00:57:30,120
Let's see what strategy Teng

1615
00:57:30,120 --> 00:57:31,540
comes up with.

1616
00:57:31,540 --> 00:57:32,980
(Follows along and steps in)

1617
00:57:33,020 --> 00:57:35,580
(A truly innocent man in his forties)

1618
00:57:35,580 --> 00:57:38,860
(Water yoga: A day of self-care)

1619
00:57:44,720 --> 00:57:46,040
You need to stand up.

1620
00:57:46,960 --> 00:57:48,320
Hold him tight.

1621
00:57:48,720 --> 00:57:49,120
One.

1622
00:57:50,420 --> 00:57:51,540
(Still not making a move?)

1623
00:57:54,740 --> 00:57:56,340
(It is time to strike)

1624
00:57:56,420 --> 00:57:58,020
(Wang Anyu)

1625
00:57:59,020 --> 00:58:00,620
(Is he sticking out too much?)

1626
00:58:02,660 --> 00:58:04,060
(Pushing backward)

1627
00:58:05,620 --> 00:58:08,340
(Quite a powerful backside)

1628
00:58:10,320 --> 00:58:10,680
Who?

1629
00:58:11,760 --> 00:58:12,440
Who?

1630
00:58:16,740 --> 00:58:18,580
(A professional surfing stance)

1631
00:58:20,860 --> 00:58:22,500
(Everyone is eliminated)

1632
00:58:25,060 --> 00:58:26,580
(Well done)

1633
00:58:27,160 --> 00:58:28,520
Who was it?

1634
00:58:28,520 --> 00:58:29,440
(Strike before they do)
Hu.

1635
00:58:29,440 --> 00:58:30,480
Who was it?

1636
00:58:30,480 --> 00:58:31,120
(It had to be him)
It came from behind.

1637
00:58:31,120 --> 00:58:31,800
Hu.

1638
00:58:32,580 --> 00:58:34,140
(Was it me, working so hard
to stay on my heels?)

1639
00:58:34,160 --> 00:58:35,280
I nearly choked to death.

1640
00:58:36,000 --> 00:58:37,200
You nearly crushed me to death.

1641
00:58:37,840 --> 00:58:40,480
I had just gotten in
when they both came down.

1642
00:58:43,440 --> 00:58:44,680
That leaves only Teng.

1643
00:58:44,680 --> 00:58:45,360
Hu.

1644
00:58:46,880 --> 00:58:48,680
